{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1787344246929,"sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","part":{"id":"prt_02604d88f001T4A8ReC8lr6kMs","messageID":"msg_02604c4fd0010rqTRjBmfEeEJ3","sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787344248973,"sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_2fe05b6393d140b9b5ccd381","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-notion/SKILL.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-notion/SKILL.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: name: mcp-notion\n3: description: Operates a Notion workspace through the official Notion MCP (@notionhq/notion-mcp-server, 24 tools) over Code Mode, fills 5 API gaps with direct Notion API calls, and routes between the headless local-stdio backend and the interactive remote OAuth backend. Carries a Notion knowledge layer (data-source model, 22 property types, relations, rollups, Formulas 2.0). Embedded registration and agent safety invariants.\n4: allowed-tools: [Bash, Edit, Glob, Grep, mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain, Read, Write]\n5: version: 0.1.0.0\n6: ---\n7: \n8: <!-- keywords: notion, notion mcp, notion api, notion database, notion data source, notion page, notion property, notion relation, notion rollup, notion formula, notion token, ntn_, notion-mcp-server, notion markdown, notion search -->\n9: \n10: # mcp-notion Skill\n11: \n12: Notion workspace operations via the **official Notion MCP** (`@notionhq/notion-mcp-server`, 24 tools) over Code Mode, plus **direct Notion API calls** for the five capabilities the MCP does not expose. It knows Notion's data model at the schema layer — data sources, 22 property types, relations, rollups, Formulas 2.0 — so an agent can create, query, and extend a workspace without guessing.\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: ## MARKDOWN + DATA-SOURCE CONTRACT — READ BEFORE ANY NOTION WRITE\n17: \n18: Two shape rules cause most Notion write failures:\n19: \n20: 1. **Page bodies vs page properties are different surfaces.** A page's *content* is a tree of **blocks** (append/update via block tools, or the markdown round-trip tools). A page's *metadata* is **properties** typed by its parent data source's schema. Writing prose into a property, or a property value into a block, fails or silently truncates.\n21: 2. **API 2.0 replaced \"databases\" with \"data sources\"** (API version `2025-09-03`). A database is now a container of one or more **data sources**; queries, schema, relations, and rollups all target a **data source id**, not a database id. Using a database id where a data-source id is required is the most common 400.\n22: \n23: Markdown round-trip tools (`retrieve-page-markdown` / `update-page-markdown`) require API version `2026-03-11` and are the token-efficient path for AI. Full detail: `references/database-model.md` and `references/mcp-tools.md`.\n24: \n25: **Failure symptom:** a `validation_error` naming `data_source_id`, or property writes that vanish, means a database id was used where a data-source id was required, or content was routed to the wrong surface.\n26: \n27: ---\n28: \n29: ## 1. WHEN TO USE\n30: \n31: ### Activation Triggers (explicit user phrases)\n32: \n33: - \"notion\", \"notion mcp\", \"notion api\", \"mcp-notion\"\n34: - \"notion page\", \"notion database\", \"notion data source\", \"query notion\"\n35: - \"create a notion page\", \"add a row\", \"notion property\", \"notion relation\", \"notion rollup\", \"notion formula\"\n36: - \"notion token\", \"notion integration\", \"ntn_\", \"notion search\"\n37: - \"upload a file to notion\", \"notion view\", \"notion async task\"\n38: \n39: ### Automatic Triggers (keyword patterns)\n40: \n41: - `notion` + any action verb (create, read, update, query, search, append, archive)\n42: - \"data source\" / \"property\" / \"rollup\" / \"relation\" in a Notion context\n43: - MCP tool names: `create-a-page`, `query-data-source`, `retrieve-a-page` (namespaced `notion.notion_<name>`)\n44: \n45: ### When NOT to Use\n46: \n47: - **Community Notion MCP servers** (suekou/mcp-notion-server, awkoy/notion-mcp-server) — this mode uses the **official** `@notionhq/notion-mcp-server` only.\n48: - **Notion→Obsidian migration mechanics** — that research lives in `specs/mcp-tooling/015-…`; this mode is the read-side inventory enabler, not the importer.\n49: - Generic markdown authoring with no Notion workspace — use `@markdown` / `sk-doc`.\n50: - Non-Notion knowledge apps (Obsidian, ClickUp docs) — wrong surface (`mcp-obsidian`, `mcp-click-up`).\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 2. SMART ROUTING\n55: \n56: ### Resource Loading Levels\n57: \n58: ```\n59: ALWAYS:    SKILL.md (this file)\n60: ON_DEMAND: references/mcp-tools.md        (24-tool catalog + Code Mode invocation)\n61:            references/api-gap-tools.md    (direct API for the 5 uncovered capabilities)\n62:            references/property-types.md   (22 property types: schema, value, filter/sort)\n63:            references/database-model.md    (data-source hierarchy, relations, rollups, Formulas 2.0)\n64:            references/troubleshooting.md   (auth, rate-limit, version, deprecation-migration)\n65: ```\n66: \n67: ### Two Decisions This Router Makes\n68: \n69: 1. **MCP vs direct API** — anything in the 24-tool surface (page/block/data-source/comment/user/search CRUD) goes through the MCP over Code Mode; the five gaps (file uploads, views, page property items, async tasks, daily-notes convention) go to direct Notion API calls.\n70: 2. **Which backend** — headless **local stdio** (`npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server`, `NOTION_TOKEN`) for Code Mode / automated sessions; **remote OAuth** (`mcp.notion.com`) only when an interactive browser session is available. Code Mode is headless, so it uses the local stdio backend.\n71: \n72: ### Backend Selection\n73: \n74: ```python\n75: def resolve_notion_backend(runtime):\n76:     \"\"\"Pick the Notion backend. Probe, never assume.\n77:       runtime.interactive   -> a browser/OAuth session is available\n78:       runtime.oauth_token   -> remote Notion MCP OAuth completed\n79:       runtime.notion_token  -> NOTION_TOKEN (ntn_...) present for Code Mode\n80:     \"\"\"\n81:     # Remote MCP is OAuth-only and CANNOT run headless. Prefer it only when a\n82:     # human/browser session is present; it adds async-task tools the local lacks.\n83:     if runtime.interactive and runtime.oauth_token:\n84:         return \"REMOTE_MCP\"      # https://mcp.notion.com/mcp (Streamable HTTP + OAuth)\n85: \n86:     # Default for Code Mode and any automated session: the local stdio server.\n87:     # Deprecated by Notion but the only headless-capable backend.\n88:     if runtime.notion_token:\n89:         return \"LOCAL_STDIO\"     # notion manual in .utcp_config.json, via Code Mode\n90: \n91:     return \"ESCALATE\"            # no auth — direct the user to INSTALL-GUIDE.md\n92: ```\n93: \n94: ### Operation-to-Tool Routing Table\n95: \n96: | Operation | Surface | Tool / call | Notes |\n97: |---|---|---|---|\n98: | Create / retrieve / update / archive a page | **MCP** | `create-a-page` / `retrieve-a-page` / `update-page-properties` / `archive-a-page` | Archive, not hard delete |\n99: | Page body as markdown (read/write) | **MCP** | `retrieve-page-markdown` / `update-page-markdown` | Needs API `2026-03-11`; token-efficient |\n100: | Append / update / delete blocks | **MCP** | block tools (`append-block-children`, `update-a-block`, `delete-a-block`, …) | Page *content* surface |\n101: | Query / retrieve / update a data source | **MCP** | `query-data-source` + data-source tools | Target the **data-source id** |\n102: | Comments (create, list) | **MCP** | comment tools | — |\n103: | Users (list, retrieve, bot) | **MCP** | user tools | — |\n104: | Search (by title) | **MCP** | `search` | **Title-only**; no full-text content search |\n105: | **File uploads** | **direct API** | `POST /v1/file_uploads` (+ send/complete) | Not in MCP — see `api-gap-tools.md` |\n106: | **Views** (create/list/query) | **direct API** | data-source view endpoints | Not in MCP |\n107: | **Page property items** (non-truncated) | **direct API** | `GET /v1/pages/{id}/properties/{prop}` | Not in MCP |\n108: | **Async tasks** (poll) | **direct API / remote MCP** | task-status endpoint | Native on remote MCP only |\n109: | **Daily notes** | **convention** | knowledge-layer pattern | No API — see `database-model.md` |\n110: \n111: ### Smart Router Pseudocode\n112: \n113: ```python\n114: from pathlib import Path\n115: \n116: SKILL_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n117: RESOURCE_BASES = (SKILL_ROOT / \"references\",)\n118: DEFAULT_RESOURCE = \"references/mcp-tools.md\"\n119: # Fallback-only: DEFAULT_RESOURCE is a defer-time suggestion, never unioned into a\n120: # route's loaded set. Scored routes load exactly RESOURCE_MAP[intent]; zero-score\n121: # routes load nothing and ask for disambiguation instead.\n122: DEFAULT_RESOURCE_SEMANTICS = \"fallback-only\"\n123: \n124: UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n125:     \"Confirm whether the request is Notion page/block ops, data-source/schema ops, an API-gap capability, install/auth, or troubleshooting\",\n126:     \"Provide the page id, data-source id, property name, or error text\",\n127:     \"Confirm whether NOTION_TOKEN (headless/Code Mode) or a remote OAuth session is available\",\n128:     \"Confirm the verification command before completing any write action\",\n129: ]\n130: \n131: INTENT_SIGNALS = {\n132:     \"NOTION_PAGES\": {\n133:         \"weight\": 5,\n134:         \"keywords\": [\"page\", \"pages\", \"block\", \"blocks\", \"append\", \"markdown\", \"content\",\n135:                      \"create page\", \"retrieve page\", \"update page\", \"archive\", \"comment\",\n136:                      \"user\", \"search\", \"title search\", \"sub-page\", \"child page\"],\n137:     },\n138:     \"NOTION_DATA\": {\n139:         \"weight\": 5,\n140:         \"keywords\": [\"database\", \"data source\", \"datasource\", \"query\", \"row\", \"rows\",\n141:                      \"relation\", \"rollup\", \"formula\", \"schema\", \"property\", \"filter\",\n142:                      \"sort\", \"data_source_id\", \"two-way relation\", \"aggregate\"],\n143:     },\n144:     \"NOTION_API_GAP\": {\n145:         \"weight\": 6,\n146:         \"keywords\": [\"file upload\", \"upload a file\", \"view\", \"views\", \"property item\",\n147:                      \"non-truncated\", \"async task\", \"poll task\", \"daily note\"],\n148:     },\n149:     \"NOTION_KNOWLEDGE\": {\n150:         \"weight\": 5,\n151:         \"keywords\": [\"property type\", \"property types\", \"select\", \"multi-select\", \"status\",\n152:                      \"formula function\", \"rollup function\", \"data model\", \"hierarchy\"],\n153:     },\n154:     \"INSTALL\": {\n155:         \"weight\": 6,\n156:         \"keywords\": [\"install\", \"setup\", \"not found\", \"not installed\", \"notion token\",\n157:                      \"ntn_\", \"integration token\", \"api token\", \"mcp config\", \"register\",\n158:                      \"configure\", \"configuration\", \"getting started\", \"onboarding\",\n159:                      \"oauth\", \"connect notion\", \"how do i install\"],\n160:     },\n161:     \"TROUBLESHOOT\": {\n162:         \"weight\": 6,\n163:         \"keywords\": [\"error\", \"failed\", \"not working\", \"401\", \"403\", \"429\", \"400\",\n164:                      \"rate limit\", \"unauthorized\", \"forbidden\", \"slow\", \"timeout\",\n165:                      \"validation_error\", \"data_source_id\", \"deprecated\", \"won't connect\",\n166:                      \"can't connect\", \"version mismatch\", \"object_not_found\"],\n167:     },\n168: }\n169: \n170: # NOTE: no \"DEFAULT\" entry — route_notion_resources() never indexes RESOURCE_MAP by\n171: # that key; the selected `intent` is always one of the six INTENT_SIGNALS keys. The\n172: # no-match case is owned by DEFAULT_RESOURCE, whose fallback-only semantics mean it is\n173: # SUGGESTED beside the disambiguation checklist, never loaded — so mcp-tools.md cannot\n174: # leak into the DATA / API_GAP / KNOWLEDGE / INSTALL / TROUBLESHOOT routes.\n175: RESOURCE_MAP = {\n176:     \"NOTION_PAGES\":     [\"references/mcp-tools.md\"],\n177:     \"NOTION_DATA\":      [\"references/database-model.md\", \"references/property-types.md\",\n178:                          \"references/mcp-tools.md\"],\n179:     \"NOTION_API_GAP\":   [\"references/api-gap-tools.md\"],\n180:     \"NOTION_KNOWLEDGE\": [\"references/property-types.md\", \"references/database-model.md\"],\n181:     \"INSTALL\":          [\"references/troubleshooting.md\"],\n182:     \"TROUBLESHOOT\":     [\"references/troubleshooting.md\"],\n183: }\n184: \n185: def discover_markdown_resources() -> set[str]:\n186:     docs = []\n187:     for base in RESOURCE_BASES:\n188:         if base.exists():\n189:             docs.extend(path for path in base.rglob(\"*.md\") if path.is_file())\n190:     return {doc.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix() for doc in docs}\n191: \n192: def _guard_in_skill(relative_path: str) -> str:\n193:     resolved = (SKILL_ROOT / relative_path).resolve()\n194:     resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT)\n195:     if resolved.suffix.lower() != \".md\":\n196:         raise ValueError(f\"Only markdown skill resources are routable: {relative_path}\")\n197:     return resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix()\n198: \n199: def load_if_available(relative_path, loaded, seen, inventory) -> None:\n200:     guarded = _guard_in_skill(relative_path)\n201:     if guarded in inventory and guarded not in seen:\n202:         load(guarded)\n203:         loaded.append(guarded)\n204:         seen.add(guarded)\n205: \n206: def route_notion_resources(request: str) -> dict:\n207:     \"\"\"Score intent labels and load available Notion reference docs.\"\"\"\n208:     inventory = discover_markdown_resources()\n209:     loaded, seen = [], set()\n210:     request_lower = request.lower()\n211: \n212:     scores = {}\n213:     for intent, config in INTENT_SIGNALS.items():\n214:         score = sum(config[\"weight\"] for kw in config[\"keywords\"] if kw in request_lower)\n215:         if score > 0:\n216:             scores[intent] = score\n217: \n218:     if not scores:\n219:         return {\n220:             \"load_level\": \"UNKNOWN_FALLBACK\",\n221:             \"needs_disambiguation\": True,\n222:             \"disambiguation_checklist\": UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST,\n223:             \"suggested_fallback\": DEFAULT_RESOURCE,\n224:             \"resources\": loaded,\n225:         }\n226: \n227:     # Error/install keywords win regardless of other signals.\n228:     if scores.get(\"TROUBLESHOOT\", 0) > 3:\n229:         intent = \"TROUBLESHOOT\"\n230:     elif scores.get(\"INSTALL\", 0) > 4:\n231:         intent = \"INSTALL\"\n232:     else:\n233:         intent = max(scores, key=scores.get)\n234: \n235:     for resource in RESOURCE_MAP[intent]:\n236:         load_if_available(resource, loaded, seen, inventory)\n237: \n238:     if not loaded:\n239:         return {\n240:             \"load_level\": \"UNKNOWN_FALLBACK\",\n241:             \"notice\": f\"No Notion reference docs available for intent '{intent}'\",\n242:             \"disambiguation_checklist\": UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST,\n243:             \"suggested_fallback\": DEFAULT_RESOURCE,\n244:             \"resources\": loaded,\n245:         }\n246: \n247:     return {\"intent\": intent, \"resources\": loaded}\n248: ```\n249: \n250: ---\n251: \n252: ## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n253: \n254: ### Backend Comparison\n255: \n256: | Dimension | Local stdio (default, headless) | Remote MCP (interactive) |\n257: |---|---|---|\n258: | **Transport** | stdio via `npx -y @notionhq/notion-mcp-server` | Streamable HTTP at `https://mcp.notion.com/mcp` |\n259: | **Auth** | `NOTION_TOKEN` (`ntn_…` internal-integration token) | OAuth (browser) |\n260: | **Headless?** | **Yes** — the only Code-Mode-capable backend | No — interactive only |\n261: | **Tool names** | `create-a-page`, `retrieve-a-page`, … | `notion-create-pages`, … + async tasks |\n262: | **Status** | **Deprecated** by Notion, still functional | **Recommended** by Notion |\n263: | **Used by** | Code Mode / automation | Human-in-the-loop clients |\n264: \n265: > **Deprecation note.** Notion is deprecating the open-source local server in favor of the remote OAuth server. Code Mode is headless, so the local stdio server is the correct (and only) choice here today; `references/troubleshooting.md` carries the local→remote migration path for when the operator moves to an interactive workflow.\n266: \n267: ### Official Notion MCP — via Code Mode (default path)\n268: \n269: The registered `notion` manual launches `@notionhq/notion-mcp-server` over **stdio** with `npx -y`. It talks to Notion's REST API with the integration's `NOTION_TOKEN`.\n270: \n271: **Prerequisites:**\n272: - Code Mode MCP configured, with the `notion` manual in `.utcp_config.json` (already registered — see INSTALL-GUIDE).\n273: - `notion_NOTION_TOKEN` (an `ntn_…` internal-integration token) available to Code Mode, and the integration granted content access to the target pages/data sources.\n274: \n275: **Configuration** (`.utcp_config.json`, `manual_call_templates`) — already applied:\n276: ```json\n277: {\n278:   \"name\": \"notion\",\n279:   \"call_template_type\": \"mcp\",\n280:   \"config\": {\n281:     \"mcpServers\": {\n282:       \"notion\": {\n283:         \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n284:         \"command\": \"npx\",\n285:         \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@notionhq/notion-mcp-server\"],\n286:         \"env\": { \"NOTION_TOKEN\": \"${notion_NOTION_TOKEN}\" }\n287:       }\n288:     }\n289:   }\n290: }\n291: ```\n292: \n293: The `notion_` env prefix matches the manual name `notion`, so `${notion_NOTION_TOKEN}` resolves. This mode documents that registration; it does not rewrite config files.\n294: \n295: **Tools:** the server exposes **24 `notion_*` tools** across 6 domains — pages (7), blocks (5), data sources (6), comments (2), users (3), search (1). Confirm every name with `tool_info()` / `list_tools()` before calling; the full catalog with per-tool inputs is in `references/mcp-tools.md`.\n296: \n297: **Invocation via Code Mode** (`call_tool_chain` takes a single `code` string):\n298: ```typescript\n299: // Code Mode namespaces each tool as notion.notion_<tool_name>. Notion tool names are\n300: // HYPHENATED (create-a-page, retrieve-a-page), so notion.notion_retrieve-a-page is invalid\n301: // JS (it parses as subtraction) — use hyphen-safe BRACKET access. VERIFY once the manual is\n302: // registered: run list_tools() to read the exact callable; Code Mode MAY instead sanitize\n303: // hyphens to underscores (notion.notion_retrieve_a_page). Bracket form is the safe default.\n304: const result = await call_tool_chain({\n305:   code: `\n306:     const hit  = await notion[\"notion_search\"]({ query: \"Roadmap\" });\n307:     const page = await notion[\"notion_retrieve-a-page\"]({ page_id: hit.results[0].id });\n308:     return page;\n309:   `,\n310: });\n311: ```\n312: \n313: ### The Five API Gaps (direct API)\n314: \n315: File uploads, views, non-truncated page property items, and async-task polling exist in the Notion REST API but **not** in the MCP tool surface; daily notes are a convention with no endpoint. Fill them with direct calls (`Authorization: Bearer $notion_NOTION_TOKEN`, `Notion-Version: 2025-09-03`, or `2026-03-11` for markdown/async). Recipes: `references/api-gap-tools.md`.\n316: \n317: **When to prefer the remote MCP:** interactive sessions where OAuth is available and async-task tools are needed. Otherwise stay on the local stdio backend.\n318: \n319: **Limitations:** search is title-only (no full-text content search); pages archive rather than hard-delete; the workspace is cloud-only (no headless filesystem); rate limit ≈ 3 req/s per integration with `Retry-After`.\n320: \n321: ---\n322: \n323: ## 4. RULES\n324: \n325: ### ✅ ALWAYS\n326: \n327: 1. **Resolve the backend before acting** — Code Mode uses the local stdio backend with `NOTION_TOKEN`; only route to the remote OAuth backend when an interactive session is genuinely available. Probe, do not assume.\n328: 2. **Target a data-source id, not a database id** — API 2.0 made data sources the primary abstraction; queries, schema, relations, and rollups all take a `data_source_id`.\n329: 3. **Route content to the right surface** — page prose → blocks (or markdown round-trip tools); metadata → typed properties. Never cross them.\n330: 4. **Confirm MCP tool names with `list_tools()` / `tool_info()`** before calling — Notion tool names are hyphenated (`create-a-page`), so the hyphen-safe callable is bracket-access `notion[\"notion_create-a-page\"]` unless `list_tools()` shows Code Mode sanitized them to underscores.\n331: 5. **Read a data source's schema before writing rows** — property types and select options are schema-defined; writing an undefined option or wrong-typed value fails.\n332: 6. **Handle the rate limit** — ≈3 req/s per integration; on `429` back off with jitter and honor `Retry-After`. Batch reads where possible.\n333: 7. **Pin the API version per operation** — `2025-09-03` for most tools, `2026-03-11` for markdown round-trip and async tasks.\n334: 8. **Preview destructive ops** — confirm the exact page/row before archive; Notion archives (recoverable) rather than hard-deletes, but bulk archives are still disruptive.\n335: \n336: ### ⛔ NEVER\n337: \n338: 1. **Never hardcode the token** — read it from `notion_NOTION_TOKEN` in the Code Mode environment; never inline `ntn_…` in a command, note, or example.\n339: 2. **Never use a community Notion MCP server as the default** — this mode is the official `@notionhq/notion-mcp-server`.\n340: 3. **Never assume the remote OAuth backend works headless** — it cannot; Code Mode must use the local stdio backend.\n341: 4. **Never auto-modify `.utcp_config.json`, `.env.example`, `opencode.json`, or hub files** — the `notion` manual is already registered there; if it needs changing, print the config for the user and never write these files programmatically.\n342: 5. **Never fabricate pages, rows, or property values** — if a query returns empty, the data source is genuinely empty or the integration lacks access. Report it.\n343: 6. **Never treat search as full-text** — `search` matches titles only; to find by content, retrieve candidate pages and inspect client-side.\n344: 7. **Never write markdown into a property field** — prose belongs in blocks or the markdown round-trip; properties are typed values.\n345: \n346: ### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n347: \n348: - No `NOTION_TOKEN` and no OAuth session → direct the user to `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` (create an internal integration, copy the `ntn_…` token to `.env`, grant content access).\n349: - A `401`/`403` → the token is missing/wrong, or the integration was not granted access to the target page/data source.\n350: - A `validation_error` naming `data_source_id` → a database id was used where a data-source id is required (2.0 migration); resolve the data source first.\n351: - Persistent `429` → the integration is over ≈3 req/s; reduce concurrency, add backoff, or batch.\n352: - The operator wants an interactive/OAuth workflow → follow the local→remote migration path in `references/troubleshooting.md`.\n353: \n354: ---\n355: \n356: ## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n357: \n358: - [ ] Code Mode `notion[\"notion_search\"]({query})` returns results (empty is valid) — confirms the manual + token work\n359: - [ ] `list_tools()` shows `notion.notion_*` entries; `tool_info(\"notion.notion_retrieve-a-page\")` resolves a live schema\n360: - [ ] `query-data-source` returns rows for a data-source id the integration can access\n361: - [ ] A page create + markdown round-trip (`update-page-markdown` → `retrieve-page-markdown`) preserves content\n362: - [ ] An API-gap call (e.g. a page-property-item `GET`) returns data with the Bearer token from the environment\n363: - [ ] `bash scripts/doctor.sh` reports Node/npx, the `notion` manual, and `notion_NOTION_TOKEN` state without mutating\n364: \n365: ---\n366: \n367: ## 6. INTEGRATION POINTS\n368: \n369: **Gate 2 (Skill Routing):** activates at ≥0.8 confidence for Notion workspace requests. The advisor matches on `notion`, `notion mcp`, `notion database`, `notion data source`, `notion page`, `notion token`.\n370: \n371: **Code Mode MCP:** the official Notion MCP tools are invoked via `mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain`; Code Mode namespaces each as `notion.notion_<tool_name>` — use hyphen-safe bracket access since Notion names are hyphenated. See `references/mcp-tools.md`.\n372: \n373: **Migration (packet 015):** this mode is the read-side inventory enabler for Notion→Obsidian migration — the same knowledge layer that operates a live workspace reads its structure to drive an Obsidian import.\n374: \n375: **Memory:** save Notion workflow context (target data-source ids, integration name, backend) with `/memory:save` when switching sessions.\n376: \n377: **Tool Usage:** Bash for direct API calls and `scripts/`; `mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain` for MCP operations; Read to load references on demand.\n378: \n379: ---\n380: \n381: ## 7. QUICK REFERENCE\n382: \n383: ### Notion MCP tool surface (24 tools, 6 domains — confirm names with `tool_info()`)\n384: \n385: | Domain | Count | Representative tools |\n386: |---|---|---|\n387: | **Pages** | 7 | create, retrieve, update, archive; markdown retrieve/update |\n388: | **Blocks** | 5 | retrieve, children, append, update, delete |\n389: | **Data sources** | 6 | query, retrieve, update, create, templates |\n390: | **Comments** | 2 | create, list |\n391: | **Users** | 3 | list, retrieve, bot |\n392: | **Search** | 1 | title search |\n393: \n394: ### The 5 gaps → direct API (`references/api-gap-tools.md`)\n395: \n396: | Gap | Endpoint family |\n397: |---|---|\n398: | File uploads | `POST /v1/file_uploads` (+ send / complete) |\n399: | Views | data-source view endpoints |\n400: | Page property items | `GET /v1/pages/{id}/properties/{prop}` |\n401: | Async tasks | task-status endpoint (native on remote MCP) |\n402: | Daily notes | convention (no endpoint) |\n403: \n404: ### Code Mode call pattern\n405: \n406: ```typescript\n407: // 24 tools, namespaced notion.notion_<tool_name>; hyphenated names → bracket access.\n408: // Confirm the exact callable with list_tools() before relying on either form.\n409: await call_tool_chain({\n410:   code: `\n411:     const ds = await notion[\"notion_query-data-source\"]({\n412:       data_source_id: \"DATA_SOURCE_ID\",\n413:       filter: { property: \"Status\", status: { equals: \"In progress\" } },\n414:     });\n415:     return ds.results.map(p => p.id);\n416:   `,\n417: });\n418: ```\n419: \n420: ---\n421: \n422: ## 8. REFERENCES AND RELATED RESOURCES\n423: \n424: **Reference Files (load on demand via router):**\n425: - `references/mcp-tools.md` — the 24-tool catalog by domain + Code Mode invocation\n426: - `references/api-gap-tools.md` — direct Notion API for the 5 uncovered capabilities\n427: - `references/property-types.md` — 22 property types: schema, value, filter/sort\n428: - `references/database-model.md` — data-source hierarchy, relations, rollups, Formulas 2.0\n429: - `references/troubleshooting.md` — auth, rate-limit, API-version, deprecation-migration\n430: \n431: Install guide (front door): [INSTALL-GUIDE.md](INSTALL-GUIDE.md) — token setup, Code Mode registration, dual-backend config.\n432: \n433: **Scripts:**\n434: - `scripts/install.sh` — prints the Code Mode manual + `notion_NOTION_TOKEN` env key (read-only)\n435: - `scripts/doctor.sh` — diagnoses Node/npx, the manual, and the token\n436: \n437: **Embedded Servers:**\n438: - `mcp-servers/notion-mcp/README.md` — official `@notionhq/notion-mcp-server` config notes (stdio, `NOTION_TOKEN`, dual-backend)\n439: \n440: **Examples:**\n441: - `examples/README.md` — Code Mode Notion workflow examples\n442: \n443: **Related Skills:**\n444: - `mcp-click-up` — structural sibling (light workflow mode)\n445: - `mcp-obsidian` — sibling knowledge app; the 015 migration counterpart\n446: - `mcp-code-mode` — Code Mode MCP orchestration (used for Notion MCP invocation)\n447: \n448: **External:**\n449: - Official Notion MCP server: https://github.com/makenotion/notion-mcp-server\n450: - Notion API reference: https://developers.notion.com/reference\n\n(End of file - total 450 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\nname: mcp-notion\ndescription: Operates a Notion workspace through the official Notion MCP (@notionhq/notion-mcp-server, 24 tools) over Code Mode, fills 5 API gaps with direct Notion API calls, and routes between the headless local-stdio backend and the interactive remote OAuth backend. Carries a Notion knowledge layer (data-source model, 22 property types, relations, rollups, Formulas 2.0). Embedded registration and agent safety invariants.\nallowed-tools: [Bash, Edit, Glob, Grep, mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain, Read, Write]\nversion: 0.1.0.0\n---\n\n<!-- keywords: notion, notion mcp, notion api, notion database, notion data source, notion page, notion property, notion relation, notion rollup, notion formula, notion token, ntn_, notion-mcp-server, notion markdown, notion search -->\n\n# mcp-notion Skill\n\nNotion workspace operations via the **official Notion MCP** (`@notionhq/notion-mcp-server`, 24 tools) over Code Mode, plus **direct Notion API calls** for the five capabilities the MCP does not expose. It knows Notion's data model at the schema layer — data sources, 22 property types, relations, rollups, Formulas 2.0 — so an agent can create, query, and extend a workspace without guessing.\n\n---\n\n## MARKDOWN + DATA-SOURCE CONTRACT — READ BEFORE ANY NOTION WRITE\n\nTwo shape rules cause most Notion write failures:\n\n1. **Page bodies vs page properties are different surfaces.** A page's *content* is a tree of **blocks** (append/update via block tools, or the markdown round-trip tools). A page's *metadata* is **properties** typed by its parent data source's schema. Writing prose into a property, or a property value into a block, fails or silently truncates.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-notion/SKILL.md","text":"---\nname: mcp-notion\ndescription: Operates a Notion workspace through the official Notion MCP (@notionhq/notion-mcp-server, 24 tools) over Code Mode, fills 5 API gaps with direct Notion API calls, and routes between the headless local-stdio backend and the interactive remote OAuth backend. Carries a Notion knowledge layer (data-source model, 22 property types, relations, rollups, Formulas 2.0). Embedded registration and agent safety invariants.\nallowed-tools: [Bash, Edit, Glob, Grep, mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain, Read, Write]\nversion: 0.1.0.0\n---\n\n<!-- keywords: notion, notion mcp, notion api, notion database, notion data source, notion page, notion property, notion relation, notion rollup, notion formula, notion token, ntn_, notion-mcp-server, notion markdown, notion search -->\n\n# mcp-notion Skill\n\nNotion workspace operations via the **official Notion MCP** (`@notionhq/notion-mcp-server`, 24 tools) over Code Mode, plus **direct Notion API calls** for the five capabilities the MCP does not expose. It knows Notion's data model at the schema layer — data sources, 22 property types, relations, rollups, Formulas 2.0 — so an agent can create, query, and extend a workspace without guessing.\n\n---\n\n## MARKDOWN + DATA-SOURCE CONTRACT — READ BEFORE ANY NOTION WRITE\n\nTwo shape rules cause most Notion write failures:\n\n1. **Page bodies vs page properties are different surfaces.** A page's *content* is a tree of **blocks** (append/update via block tools, or the markdown round-trip tools). A page's *metadata* is **properties** typed by its parent data source's schema. Writing prose into a property, or a property value into a block, fails or silently truncates.\n2. **API 2.0 replaced \"databases\" with \"data sources\"** (API version `2025-09-03`). A database is now a container of one or more **data sources**; queries, schema, relations, and rollups all target a **data source id**, not a database id. Using a database id where a data-source id is required is the most common 400.\n\nMarkdown round-trip tools (`retrieve-page-markdown` / `update-page-markdown`) require API version `2026-03-11` and are the token-efficient path for AI. Full detail: `references/database-model.md` and `references/mcp-tools.md`.\n\n**Failure symptom:** a `validation_error` naming `data_source_id`, or property writes that vanish, means a database id was used where a data-source id was required, or content was routed to the wrong surface.\n\n---\n\n## 1. WHEN TO USE\n\n### Activation Triggers (explicit user phrases)\n\n- \"notion\", \"notion mcp\", \"notion api\", \"mcp-notion\"\n- \"notion page\", \"notion database\", \"notion data source\", \"query notion\"\n- \"create a notion page\", \"add a row\", \"notion property\", \"notion relation\", \"notion rollup\", \"notion formula\"\n- \"notion token\", \"notion integration\", \"ntn_\", \"notion search\"\n- \"upload a file to notion\", \"notion view\", \"notion async task\"\n\n### Automatic Triggers (keyword patterns)\n\n- `notion` + any action verb (create, read, update, query, search, append, archive)\n- \"data source\" / \"property\" / \"rollup\" / \"relation\" in a Notion context\n- MCP tool names: `create-a-page`, `query-data-source`, `retrieve-a-page` (namespaced `notion.notion_<name>`)\n\n### When NOT to Use\n\n- **Community Notion MCP servers** (suekou/mcp-notion-server, awkoy/notion-mcp-server) — this mode uses the **official** `@notionhq/notion-mcp-server` only.\n- **Notion→Obsidian migration mechanics** — that research lives in `specs/mcp-tooling/015-…`; this mode is the read-side inventory enabler, not the importer.\n- Generic markdown authoring with no Notion workspace — use `@markdown` / `sk-doc`.\n- Non-Notion knowledge apps (Obsidian, ClickUp docs) — wrong surface (`mcp-obsidian`, `mcp-click-up`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. SMART ROUTING\n\n### Resource Loading Levels\n\n```\nALWAYS:    SKILL.md (this file)\nON_DEMAND: references/mcp-tools.md        (24-tool catalog + Code Mode invocation)\n           references/api-gap-tools.md    (direct API for the 5 uncovered capabilities)\n           references/property-types.md   (22 property types: schema, value, filter/sort)\n           references/database-model.md    (data-source hierarchy, relations, rollups, Formulas 2.0)\n           references/troubleshooting.md   (auth, rate-limit, version, deprecation-migration)\n```\n\n### Two Decisions This Router Makes\n\n1. **MCP vs direct API** — anything in the 24-tool surface (page/block/data-source/comment/user/search CRUD) goes through the MCP over Code Mode; the five gaps (file uploads, views, page property items, async tasks, daily-notes convention) go to direct Notion API calls.\n2. **Which backend** — headless **local stdio** (`npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server`, `NOTION_TOKEN`) for Code Mode / automated sessions; **remote OAuth** (`mcp.notion.com`) only when an interactive browser session is available. Code Mode is headless, so it uses the local stdio backend.\n\n### Backend Selection\n\n```python\ndef resolve_notion_backend(runtime):\n    \"\"\"Pick the Notion backend. Probe, never assume.\n      runtime.interactive   -> a browser/OAuth session is available\n      runtime.oauth_token   -> remote Notion MCP OAuth completed\n      runtime.notion_token  -> NOTION_TOKEN (ntn_...) present for Code Mode\n    \"\"\"\n    # Remote MCP is OAuth-only and CANNOT run headless. Prefer it only when a\n    # human/browser session is present; it adds async-task tools the local lacks.\n    if runtime.interactive and runtime.oauth_token:\n        return \"REMOTE_MCP\"      # https://mcp.notion.com/mcp (Streamable HTTP + OAuth)\n\n    # Default for Code Mode and any automated session: the local stdio server.\n    # Deprecated by Notion but the only headless-capable backend.\n    if runtime.notion_token:\n        return \"LOCAL_STDIO\"     # notion manual in .utcp_config.json, via Code Mode\n\n    return \"ESCALATE\"            # no auth — direct the user to INSTALL-GUIDE.md\n```\n\n### Operation-to-Tool Routing Table\n\n| Operation | Surface | Tool / call | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Create / retrieve / update / archive a page | **MCP** | `create-a-page` / `retrieve-a-page` / `update-page-properties` / `archive-a-page` | Archive, not hard delete |\n| Page body as markdown (read/write) | **MCP** | `retrieve-page-markdown` / `update-page-markdown` | Needs API `2026-03-11`; token-efficient |\n| Append / update / delete blocks | **MCP** | block tools (`append-block-children`, `update-a-block`, `delete-a-block`, …) | Page *content* surface |\n| Query / retrieve / update a data source | **MCP** | `query-data-source` + data-source tools | Target the **data-source id** |\n| Comments (create, list) | **MCP** | comment tools | — |\n| Users (list, retrieve, bot) | **MCP** | user tools | — |\n| Search (by title) | **MCP** | `search` | **Title-only**; no full-text content search |\n| **File uploads** | **direct API** | `POST /v1/file_uploads` (+ send/complete) | Not in MCP — see `api-gap-tools.md` |\n| **Views** (create/list/query) | **direct API** | data-source view endpoints | Not in MCP |\n| **Page property items** (non-truncated) | **direct API** | `GET /v1/pages/{id}/properties/{prop}` | Not in MCP |\n| **Async tasks** (poll) | **direct API / remote MCP** | task-status endpoint | Native on remote MCP only |\n| **Daily notes** | **convention** | knowledge-layer pattern | No API — see `database-model.md` |\n\n### Smart Router Pseudocode\n\n```python\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSKILL_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nRESOURCE_BASES = (SKILL_ROOT / \"references\",)\nDEFAULT_RESOURCE = \"references/mcp-tools.md\"\n# Fallback-only: DEFAULT_RESOURCE is a defer-time suggestion, never unioned into a\n# route's loaded set. Scored routes load exactly RESOURCE_MAP[intent]; zero-score\n# routes load nothing and ask for disambiguation instead.\nDEFAULT_RESOURCE_SEMANTICS = \"fallback-only\"\n\nUNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n    \"Confirm whether the request is Notion page/block ops, data-source/schema ops, an API-gap capability, install/auth, or troubleshooting\",\n    \"Provide the page id, data-source id, property name, or error text\",\n    \"Confirm whether NOTION_TOKEN (headless/Code Mode) or a remote OAuth session is available\",\n    \"Confirm the verification command before completing any write action\",\n]\n\nINTENT_SIGNALS = {\n    \"NOTION_PAGES\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"page\", \"pages\", \"block\", \"blocks\", \"append\", \"markdown\", \"content\",\n                     \"create page\", \"retrieve page\", \"update page\", \"archive\", \"comment\",\n                     \"user\", \"search\", \"title search\", \"sub-page\", \"child page\"],\n    },\n    \"NOTION_DATA\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"database\", \"data source\", \"datasource\", \"query\", \"row\", \"rows\",\n                     \"relation\", \"rollup\", \"formula\", \"schema\", \"property\", \"filter\",\n                     \"sort\", \"data_source_id\", \"two-way relation\", \"aggregate\"],\n    },\n    \"NOTION_API_GAP\": {\n        \"weight\": 6,\n        \"keywords\": [\"file upload\", \"upload a file\", \"view\", \"views\", \"property item\",\n                     \"non-truncated\", \"async task\", \"poll task\", \"daily note\"],\n    },\n    \"NOTION_KNOWLEDGE\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"property type\", \"property types\", \"select\", \"multi-select\", \"status\",\n                     \"formula function\", \"rollup function\", \"data model\", \"hierarchy\"],\n    },\n    \"INSTALL\": {\n        \"weight\": 6,\n        \"keywords\": [\"install\", \"setup\", \"not found\", \"not installed\", \"notion token\",\n                     \"ntn_\", \"integration token\", \"api token\", \"mcp config\", \"register\",\n                     \"configure\", \"configuration\", \"getting started\", \"onboarding\",\n                     \"oauth\", \"connect notion\", \"how do i install\"],\n    },\n    \"TROUBLESHOOT\": {\n        \"weight\": 6,\n        \"keywords\": [\"error\", \"failed\", \"not working\", \"401\", \"403\", \"429\", \"400\",\n                     \"rate limit\", \"unauthorized\", \"forbidden\", \"slow\", \"timeout\",\n                     \"validation_error\", \"data_source_id\", \"deprecated\", \"won't connect\",\n                     \"can't connect\", \"version mismatch\", \"object_not_found\"],\n    },\n}\n\n# NOTE: no \"DEFAULT\" entry — route_notion_resources() never indexes RESOURCE_MAP by\n# that key; the selected `intent` is always one of the six INTENT_SIGNALS keys. The\n# no-match case is owned by DEFAULT_RESOURCE, whose fallback-only semantics mean it is\n# SUGGESTED beside the disambiguation checklist, never loaded — so mcp-tools.md cannot\n# leak into the DATA / API_GAP / KNOWLEDGE / INSTALL / TROUBLESHOOT routes.\nRESOURCE_MAP = {\n    \"NOTION_PAGES\":     [\"references/mcp-tools.md\"],\n    \"NOTION_DATA\":      [\"references/database-model.md\", \"references/property-types.md\",\n                         \"references/mcp-tools.md\"],\n    \"NOTION_API_GAP\":   [\"references/api-gap-tools.md\"],\n    \"NOTION_KNOWLEDGE\": [\"references/property-types.md\", \"references/database-model.md\"],\n    \"INSTALL\":          [\"references/troubleshooting.md\"],\n    \"TROUBLESHOOT\":     [\"references/troubleshooting.md\"],\n}\n\ndef discover_markdown_resources() -> set[str]:\n    docs = []\n    for base in RESOURCE_BASES:\n        if base.exists():\n            docs.extend(path for path in base.rglob(\"*.md\") if path.is_file())\n    return {doc.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix() for doc in docs}\n\ndef _guard_in_skill(relative_path: str) -> str:\n    resolved = (SKILL_ROOT / relative_path).resolve()\n    resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT)\n    if resolved.suffix.lower() != \".md\":\n        raise ValueError(f\"Only markdown skill resources are routable: {relative_path}\")\n    return resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix()\n\ndef load_if_available(relative_path, loaded, seen, inventory) -> None:\n    guarded = _guard_in_skill(relative_path)\n    if guarded in inventory and guarded not in seen:\n        load(guarded)\n        loaded.append(guarded)\n        seen.add(guarded)\n\ndef route_notion_resources(request: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Score intent labels and load available Notion reference docs.\"\"\"\n    inventory = discover_markdown_resources()\n    loaded, seen = [], set()\n    request_lower = request.lower()\n\n    scores = {}\n    for intent, config in INTENT_SIGNALS.items():\n        score = sum(config[\"weight\"] for kw in config[\"keywords\"] if kw in request_lower)\n        if score > 0:\n            scores[intent] = score\n\n    if not scores:\n        return {\n            \"load_level\": \"UNKNOWN_FALLBACK\",\n            \"needs_disambiguation\": True,\n            \"disambiguation_checklist\": UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST,\n            \"suggested_fallback\": DEFAULT_RESOURCE,\n            \"resources\": loaded,\n        }\n\n    # Error/install keywords win regardless of other signals.\n    if scores.get(\"TROUBLESHOOT\", 0) > 3:\n        intent = \"TROUBLESHOOT\"\n    elif scores.get(\"INSTALL\", 0) > 4:\n        intent = \"INSTALL\"\n    else:\n        intent = max(scores, key=scores.get)\n\n    for resource in RESOURCE_MAP[intent]:\n        load_if_available(resource, loaded, seen, inventory)\n\n    if not loaded:\n        return {\n            \"load_level\": \"UNKNOWN_FALLBACK\",\n            \"notice\": f\"No Notion reference docs available for intent '{intent}'\",\n            \"disambiguation_checklist\": UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST,\n            \"suggested_fallback\": DEFAULT_RESOURCE,\n            \"resources\": loaded,\n        }\n\n    return {\"intent\": intent, \"resources\": loaded}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Backend Comparison\n\n| Dimension | Local stdio (default, headless) | Remote MCP (interactive) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Transport** | stdio via `npx -y @notionhq/notion-mcp-server` | Streamable HTTP at `https://mcp.notion.com/mcp` |\n| **Auth** | `NOTION_TOKEN` (`ntn_…` internal-integration token) | OAuth (browser) |\n| **Headless?** | **Yes** — the only Code-Mode-capable backend | No — interactive only |\n| **Tool names** | `create-a-page`, `retrieve-a-page`, … | `notion-create-pages`, … + async tasks |\n| **Status** | **Deprecated** by Notion, still functional | **Recommended** by Notion |\n| **Used by** | Code Mode / automation | Human-in-the-loop clients |\n\n> **Deprecation note.** Notion is deprecating the open-source local server in favor of the remote OAuth server. Code Mode is headless, so the local stdio server is the correct (and only) choice here today; `references/troubleshooting.md` carries the local→remote migration path for when the operator moves to an interactive workflow.\n\n### Official Notion MCP — via Code Mode (default path)\n\nThe registered `notion` manual launches `@notionhq/notion-mcp-server` over **stdio** with `npx -y`. It talks to Notion's REST API with the integration's `NOTION_TOKEN`.\n\n**Prerequisites:**\n- Code Mode MCP configured, with the `notion` manual in `.utcp_config.json` (already registered — see INSTALL-GUIDE).\n- `notion_NOTION_TOKEN` (an `ntn_…` internal-integration token) available to Code Mode, and the integration granted content access to the target pages/data sources.\n\n**Configuration** (`.utcp_config.json`, `manual_call_templates`) — already applied:\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"notion\",\n  \"call_template_type\": \"mcp\",\n  \"config\": {\n    \"mcpServers\": {\n      \"notion\": {\n        \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n        \"command\": \"npx\",\n        \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@notionhq/notion-mcp-server\"],\n        \"env\": { \"NOTION_TOKEN\": \"${notion_NOTION_TOKEN}\" }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe `notion_` env prefix matches the manual name `notion`, so `${notion_NOTION_TOKEN}` resolves. This mode documents that registration; it does not rewrite config files.\n\n**Tools:** the server exposes **24 `notion_*` tools** across 6 domains — pages (7), blocks (5), data sources (6), comments (2), users (3), search (1). Confirm every name with `tool_info()` / `list_tools()` before calling; the full catalog with per-tool inputs is in `references/mcp-tools.md`.\n\n**Invocation via Code Mode** (`call_tool_chain` takes a single `code` string):\n```typescript\n// Code Mode namespaces each tool as notion.notion_<tool_name>. Notion tool names are\n// HYPHENATED (create-a-page, retrieve-a-page), so notion.notion_retrieve-a-page is invalid\n// JS (it parses as subtraction) — use hyphen-safe BRACKET access. VERIFY once the manual is\n// registered: run list_tools() to read the exact callable; Code Mode MAY instead sanitize\n// hyphens to underscores (notion.notion_retrieve_a_page). Bracket form is the safe default.\nconst result = await call_tool_chain({\n  code: `\n    const hit  = await notion[\"notion_search\"]({ query: \"Roadmap\" });\n    const page = await notion[\"notion_retrieve-a-page\"]({ page_id: hit.results[0].id });\n    return page;\n  `,\n});\n```\n\n### The Five API Gaps (direct API)\n\nFile uploads, views, non-truncated page property items, and async-task polling exist in the Notion REST API but **not** in the MCP tool surface; daily notes are a convention with no endpoint. Fill them with direct calls (`Authorization: Bearer $notion_NOTION_TOKEN`, `Notion-Version: 2025-09-03`, or `2026-03-11` for markdown/async). Recipes: `references/api-gap-tools.md`.\n\n**When to prefer the remote MCP:** interactive sessions where OAuth is available and async-task tools are needed. Otherwise stay on the local stdio backend.\n\n**Limitations:** search is title-only (no full-text content search); pages archive rather than hard-delete; the workspace is cloud-only (no headless filesystem); rate limit ≈ 3 req/s per integration with `Retry-After`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. RULES\n\n### ✅ ALWAYS\n\n1. **Resolve the backend before acting** — Code Mode uses the local stdio backend with `NOTION_TOKEN`; only route to the remote OAuth backend when an interactive session is genuinely available. Probe, do not assume.\n2. **Target a data-source id, not a database id** — API 2.0 made data sources the primary abstraction; queries, schema, relations, and rollups all take a `data_source_id`.\n3. **Route content to the right surface** — page prose → blocks (or markdown round-trip tools); metadata → typed properties. Never cross them.\n4. **Confirm MCP tool names with `list_tools()` / `tool_info()`** before calling — Notion tool names are hyphenated (`create-a-page`), so the hyphen-safe callable is bracket-access `notion[\"notion_create-a-page\"]` unless `list_tools()` shows Code Mode sanitized them to underscores.\n5. **Read a data source's schema before writing rows** — property types and select options are schema-defined; writing an undefined option or wrong-typed value fails.\n6. **Handle the rate limit** — ≈3 req/s per integration; on `429` back off with jitter and honor `Retry-After`. Batch reads where possible.\n7. **Pin the API version per operation** — `2025-09-03` for most tools, `2026-03-11` for markdown round-trip and async tasks.\n8. **Preview destructive ops** — confirm the exact page/row before archive; Notion archives (recoverable) rather than hard-deletes, but bulk archives are still disruptive.\n\n### ⛔ NEVER\n\n1. **Never hardcode the token** — read it from `notion_NOTION_TOKEN` in the Code Mode environment; never inline `ntn_…` in a command, note, or example.\n2. **Never use a community Notion MCP server as the default** — this mode is the official `@notionhq/notion-mcp-server`.\n3. **Never assume the remote OAuth backend works headless** — it cannot; Code Mode must use the local stdio backend.\n4. **Never auto-modify `.utcp_config.json`, `.env.example`, `opencode.json`, or hub files** — the `notion` manual is already registered there; if it needs changing, print the config for the user and never write these files programmatically.\n5. **Never fabricate pages, rows, or property values** — if a query returns empty, the data source is genuinely empty or the integration lacks access. Report it.\n6. **Never treat search as full-text** — `search` matches titles only; to find by content, retrieve candidate pages and inspect client-side.\n7. **Never write markdown into a property field** — prose belongs in blocks or the markdown round-trip; properties are typed values.\n\n### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n\n- No `NOTION_TOKEN` and no OAuth session → direct the user to `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` (create an internal integration, copy the `ntn_…` token to `.env`, grant content access).\n- A `401`/`403` → the token is missing/wrong, or the integration was not granted access to the target page/data source.\n- A `validation_error` naming `data_source_id` → a database id was used where a data-source id is required (2.0 migration); resolve the data source first.\n- Persistent `429` → the integration is over ≈3 req/s; reduce concurrency, add backoff, or batch.\n- The operator wants an interactive/OAuth workflow → follow the local→remote migration path in `references/troubleshooting.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- [ ] Code Mode `notion[\"notion_search\"]({query})` returns results (empty is valid) — confirms the manual + token work\n- [ ] `list_tools()` shows `notion.notion_*` entries; `tool_info(\"notion.notion_retrieve-a-page\")` resolves a live schema\n- [ ] `query-data-source` returns rows for a data-source id the integration can access\n- [ ] A page create + markdown round-trip (`update-page-markdown` → `retrieve-page-markdown`) preserves content\n- [ ] An API-gap call (e.g. a page-property-item `GET`) returns data with the Bearer token from the environment\n- [ ] `bash scripts/doctor.sh` reports Node/npx, the `notion` manual, and `notion_NOTION_TOKEN` state without mutating\n\n---\n\n## 6. INTEGRATION POINTS\n\n**Gate 2 (Skill Routing):** activates at ≥0.8 confidence for Notion workspace requests. The advisor matches on `notion`, `notion mcp`, `notion database`, `notion data source`, `notion page`, `notion token`.\n\n**Code Mode MCP:** the official Notion MCP tools are invoked via `mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain`; Code Mode namespaces each as `notion.notion_<tool_name>` — use hyphen-safe bracket access since Notion names are hyphenated. See `references/mcp-tools.md`.\n\n**Migration (packet 015):** this mode is the read-side inventory enabler for Notion→Obsidian migration — the same knowledge layer that operates a live workspace reads its structure to drive an Obsidian import.\n\n**Memory:** save Notion workflow context (target data-source ids, integration name, backend) with `/memory:save` when switching sessions.\n\n**Tool Usage:** Bash for direct API calls and `scripts/`; `mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain` for MCP operations; Read to load references on demand.\n\n---\n\n## 7. QUICK REFERENCE\n\n### Notion MCP tool surface (24 tools, 6 domains — confirm names with `tool_info()`)\n\n| Domain | Count | Representative tools |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Pages** | 7 | create, retrieve, update, archive; markdown retrieve/update |\n| **Blocks** | 5 | retrieve, children, append, update, delete |\n| **Data sources** | 6 | query, retrieve, update, create, templates |\n| **Comments** | 2 | create, list |\n| **Users** | 3 | list, retrieve, bot |\n| **Search** | 1 | title search |\n\n### The 5 gaps → direct API (`references/api-gap-tools.md`)\n\n| Gap | Endpoint family |\n|---|---|\n| File uploads | `POST /v1/file_uploads` (+ send / complete) |\n| Views | data-source view endpoints |\n| Page property items | `GET /v1/pages/{id}/properties/{prop}` |\n| Async tasks | task-status endpoint (native on remote MCP) |\n| Daily notes | convention (no endpoint) |\n\n### Code Mode call pattern\n\n```typescript\n// 24 tools, namespaced notion.notion_<tool_name>; hyphenated names → bracket access.\n// Confirm the exact callable with list_tools() before relying on either form.\nawait call_tool_chain({\n  code: `\n    const ds = await notion[\"notion_query-data-source\"]({\n      data_source_id: \"DATA_SOURCE_ID\",\n      filter: { property: \"Status\", status: { equals: \"In progress\" } },\n    });\n    return ds.results.map(p => p.id);\n  `,\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. REFERENCES AND RELATED RESOURCES\n\n**Reference Files (load on demand via router):**\n- `references/mcp-tools.md` — the 24-tool catalog by domain + Code Mode invocation\n- `references/api-gap-tools.md` — direct Notion API for the 5 uncovered capabilities\n- `references/property-types.md` — 22 property types: schema, value, filter/sort\n- `references/database-model.md` — data-source hierarchy, relations, rollups, Formulas 2.0\n- `references/troubleshooting.md` — auth, rate-limit, API-version, deprecation-migration\n\nInstall guide (front door): [INSTALL-GUIDE.md](INSTALL-GUIDE.md) — token setup, Code Mode registration, dual-backend config.\n\n**Scripts:**\n- `scripts/install.sh` — prints the Code Mode manual + `notion_NOTION_TOKEN` env key (read-only)\n- `scripts/doctor.sh` — diagnoses Node/npx, the manual, and the token\n\n**Embedded Servers:**\n- `mcp-servers/notion-mcp/README.md` — official `@notionhq/notion-mcp-server` config notes (stdio, `NOTION_TOKEN`, dual-backend)\n\n**Examples:**\n- `examples/README.md` — Code Mode Notion workflow examples\n\n**Related Skills:**\n- `mcp-click-up` — structural sibling (light workflow mode)\n- `mcp-obsidian` — sibling knowledge app; the 015 migration counterpart\n- `mcp-code-mode` — Code Mode MCP orchestration (used for Notion MCP invocation)\n\n**External:**\n- Official Notion MCP server: https://github.com/makenotion/notion-mcp-server\n- Notion API reference: https://developers.notion.com/reference","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":450,"totalLines":450,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-notion/SKILL.md","time":{"start":1787344248959,"end":1787344248971}},"id":"prt_02604de1c001t6xJ7bzy3zRm86","sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","messageID":"msg_02604c4fd0010rqTRjBmfEeEJ3"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787344249703,"sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_78961344cac94730a82bed79","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-obsidian/SKILL.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-obsidian/SKILL.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: name: mcp-obsidian\n3: description: Makes AI use inside Obsidian effective: vault and note operations across the headless notesmd-cli, the app-backed official obsidian CLI, and the cyanheads MCP, plus deep plugin and theme knowledge (Beancount, Tables, BRAT, Health.md, Iconic, Charts, Dataview, Excalidraw, Git, Outliner, Minimal) operated at the file layer. Embedded install and agent safety invariants.\n4: allowed-tools: [Bash, Edit, Glob, Grep, mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain, Read, Write]\n5: version: 0.18.0.0\n6: ---\n7: \n8: <!-- keywords: obsidian, obsidian vault, notesmd-cli, obsidian-mcp, note management, markdown notes, beancount, local rest api, health-md, health data, iconic, icon rules, iconic rulebook, icon automation, file icons, folder icons, iconic data json, iconic ruleset, iconic-rules.full.json, iconic-rules.full.md, data.json, charts, chart render block, dataview, dql, dataviewjs, inline field, excalidraw, excalidraw.md, drawing note, obsidian-git, vault git, auto backup, outliner, list editing, minimal theme, css theme, theme snippet -->\n9: \n10: # mcp-obsidian Skill\n11: \n12: The skill that makes AI use inside Obsidian effective. It operates notes and vaults through three surfaces (headless `notesmd-cli`, the app-backed official `obsidian` CLI, and the cyanheads MCP) and knows the eleven plugin and theme file formats at the file layer, so an agent can read, write, search, and extend what the vault contains without guessing.\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: ## 1. WHEN TO USE\n17: \n18: ### Activation Triggers (explicit user phrases)\n19: \n20: - \"obsidian\", \"obsidian vault\", \"notesmd-cli\", \"obsidian-mcp\", \"mcp-obsidian\"\n21: - \"note\", \"notes\", \"markdown note\", \"daily note\", \"vault\"\n22: - \"create a note\", \"open a note\", \"search notes\", \"search my vault\"\n23: - \"add a tag to a note\", \"manage frontmatter\", \"delete a note\", \"move a note\"\n24: - \"obsidian plugin\", \"beancount\", \"beancount finance\", \"obsidian tables\", \"brat\"\n25: - \"health\", \"health data\", \"apple health\", \"health chart\", \"health-md\", \"health.md\"\n26: - \"iconic\", \"icons\", \"icon color\", \"file icons\", \"folder icons\", \"icon rules\", \"iconic rulebook\", \"iconic ruleset\", \"iconic data json\", \"icon automation\"\n27: - \"local rest api\", \"obsidian api key\"\n28: \n29: ### Automatic Triggers (keyword patterns)\n30: \n31: - `notesmd-cli` or `obsidian` (the CLI binary) appears in the request\n32: - `obsidian` + any action verb (create, open, search, list, print, move, delete, tag)\n33: - \"vault\" in a note-management context\n34: - \"daily note\" or \"note frontmatter\" in a personal-knowledge context\n35: - MCP tool names: `obsidian_get_note`, `obsidian_write_note`, `obsidian_search_notes`\n36: \n37: ### When NOT to Use\n38: \n39: - **StevenStavrakis `obsidian-mcp`** — a different (filesystem-based) MCP server; this skill's MCP path uses the cyanheads `obsidian-mcp-server`. The Stavrakis server is documented only as the headless MCP alternative.\n40: - Generic markdown authoring with no Obsidian vault — use `@markdown` / `sk-doc`.\n41: - Non-Obsidian note apps (Notion, Bear, Apple Notes) — wrong surface.\n42: - Editing arbitrary repo files that merely happen to be markdown — use `Read`/`Edit` directly.\n43: \n44: ---\n45: \n46: ## 2. SMART ROUTING\n47: \n48: ### Resource Loading Levels\n49: \n50: ```\n51: ALWAYS:    SKILL.md (this file)\n52: ON_DEMAND: references/obsidian-cli-commands.md          (notesmd-cli + official obsidian CLI command details)\n53:            references/mcp-tools.md                      (cyanheads MCP tool catalog + invocation)\n54:            references/troubleshooting.md                (error, auth, REST API, or install issue detected)\n55:            Plugin operation logic:\n56:              references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md (plugin-driven note automation)\n57:            Beancount Finance:\n58:              references/plugins/beancount-finance/beancount-finance.md      (plugin index)\n59:              references/plugins/beancount-finance/data-model.md\n60:              references/plugins/beancount-finance/workflows.md\n61:              references/plugins/beancount-finance/troubleshooting.md\n62:            Obsidian Tables:\n63:              references/plugins/obsidian-tables/obsidian-tables.md         (plugin index)\n64:              references/plugins/obsidian-tables/data-model.md\n65:              references/plugins/obsidian-tables/workflows.md\n66:              references/plugins/obsidian-tables/troubleshooting.md\n67:            Obsidian42 BRAT:\n68:              references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/obsidian42-brat.md         (plugin index)\n69:              references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/data-model.md\n70:              references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/workflows.md\n71:              references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/troubleshooting.md\n72:            Health.md Visualizations:\n73:              references/plugins/health-md/health-md.md                   (plugin index)\n74:              references/plugins/health-md/data-model.md\n75:              references/plugins/health-md/workflows.md\n76:              references/plugins/health-md/troubleshooting.md\n77:            Iconic:\n78:              references/plugins/iconic/iconic.md                         (plugin index)\n79:              references/plugins/iconic/data-model.md\n80:              references/plugins/iconic/workflows.md\n81:              references/plugins/iconic/troubleshooting.md\n82:            Charts:\n83:              references/plugins/charts/charts.md                         (plugin index)\n84:              references/plugins/charts/data-model.md\n85:              references/plugins/charts/workflows.md\n86:              references/plugins/charts/troubleshooting.md\n87:            Dataview:\n88:              references/plugins/dataview/dataview.md                     (plugin index)\n89:              references/plugins/dataview/data-model.md\n90:              references/plugins/dataview/workflows.md\n91:              references/plugins/dataview/troubleshooting.md\n92:            Excalidraw:\n93:              references/plugins/excalidraw/excalidraw.md                 (plugin index)\n94:              references/plugins/excalidraw/data-model.md\n95:              references/plugins/excalidraw/workflows.md\n96:              references/plugins/excalidraw/troubleshooting.md\n97:            Obsidian Git:\n98:              references/plugins/git/git.md                               (plugin index)\n99:              references/plugins/git/data-model.md\n100:              references/plugins/git/workflows.md\n101:              references/plugins/git/troubleshooting.md\n102:            Outliner:\n103:              references/plugins/outliner/outliner.md                     (plugin index)\n104:              references/plugins/outliner/data-model.md\n105:              references/plugins/outliner/workflows.md\n106:              references/plugins/outliner/troubleshooting.md\n107:            Minimal (theme):\n108:              references/plugins/minimal/minimal.md                       (plugin index)\n109:              references/plugins/minimal/data-model.md\n110:              references/plugins/minimal/workflows.md\n111:              references/plugins/minimal/troubleshooting.md\n112: ```\n113: \n114: ### Two Decisions This Router Makes\n115: \n116: 1. **CLI vs MCP** — filesystem/terminal work goes to a CLI; live-app note reads/writes/tags/search go to the MCP.\n117: 2. **Which CLI profile** — headless `notesmd-cli` (default, no running app) vs the app-backed official `obsidian` CLI (a remote control for a running desktop app).\n118: \n119: ### Execution Profile Selection\n120: \n121: | Surface | Binary / transport | Needs a running app? | Best for |\n122: |---|---|---|---|\n123: | **Headless CLI** | `notesmd-cli` (Bash) | No — operates on the vault filesystem | Daily note ops anywhere: open, daily, search, create, list, print, move, delete, frontmatter, vault management |\n124: | **App-backed CLI** | `obsidian` (Bash) | Yes — launches/controls the desktop app | In-app actions: opening notes in the live UI, `obsidian://` URI actions, app-context commands |\n125: | **MCP** | `obsidian.obsidian_*` via Code Mode | Yes — plus Local REST API + `OBSIDIAN_API_KEY` | Structured note reads/writes, tag management, semantic/global search over a live vault |\n126: \n127: ```python\n128: def resolve_execution_profile(request, runtime):\n129:     \"\"\"Pick the execution surface for an Obsidian operation.\n130: \n131:     Best-effort runtime probes — never fabricated:\n132:       runtime.app_running   -> an Obsidian desktop app is live\n133:       runtime.rest_api_up   -> Local REST API plugin reachable on OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL\n134:       runtime.api_key       -> OBSIDIAN_API_KEY present in the Code Mode environment\n135:     \"\"\"\n136:     # MCP path needs a live app + Local REST API + token. It is the only surface\n137:     # for structured note reads/writes, tag management and global/semantic search.\n138:     if wants_structured_note_ops(request) and runtime.app_running \\\n139:             and runtime.rest_api_up and runtime.api_key:\n140:         return \"MCP\"            # cyanheads obsidian-mcp-server via Code Mode\n141: \n142:     # The official obsidian CLI is a remote control for a RUNNING app; use it only\n143:     # for in-app actions (open in UI, obsidian:// URIs) when the app is up.\n144:     if runtime.app_running and needs_app_command(request):\n145:         return \"OBSIDIAN_CLI\"   # official `obsidian` CLI\n146: \n147:     # Default: headless, filesystem-only, works with no running app or token.\n148:     return \"NOTESMD_CLI\"        # Yakitrak notesmd-cli\n149: ```\n150: \n151: ### Operation-to-Tool Routing Table\n152: \n153: | Operation | Primary Surface | Command / Tool | Alternative |\n154: |---|---|---|---|\n155: | Open a note | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli open \"<name>\"` | `obsidian` CLI (in live app) |\n156: | Open/append daily note | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli daily` | MCP `obsidian_write_note` |\n157: | Search by note name | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli list` + filter (`search` title-lookup is broken in v0.3.6) | MCP `obsidian_search_notes` |\n158: | Search note contents | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli search-content \"<query>\"` | MCP `obsidian_search_notes` |\n159: | List notes | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli list` | MCP `obsidian_search_notes` |\n160: | Print a note to stdout | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli print \"<name>\"` | MCP `obsidian_get_note` |\n161: | Create a note | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli create \"<name>\"` | MCP `obsidian_write_note` |\n162: | Move / rename a note | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli move \"<a>\" \"<b>\"` | n/a |\n163: | Delete a note | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli delete \"<name>\"` | MCP `obsidian_delete_note` |\n164: | Edit frontmatter | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli frontmatter \"<name>\"` | MCP `obsidian_manage_tags` |\n165: | Vault registration | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli add-vault` / `set-default-vault` | n/a |\n166: | **Structured note read** | **MCP** | `obsidian_get_note` | notesmd-cli `print` |\n167: | **Structured note write** | **MCP** | `obsidian_write_note` | notesmd-cli `create` |\n168: | **Tag management** | **MCP** | `obsidian_manage_tags` | notesmd-cli `frontmatter` |\n169: | **Global / semantic search** | **MCP** | `obsidian_search_notes` | notesmd-cli `search-content` |\n170: | **In-app open / URI action** | **obsidian CLI** | `obsidian \"<vault/path>\"` | n/a |\n171: | **Plugin-driven automation** | reference | `references/plugins/*` | n/a |\n172: \n173: ### Smart Router Pseudocode\n174: \n175: ```python\n176: from pathlib import Path\n177: \n178: SKILL_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n179: RESOURCE_BASES = (SKILL_ROOT / \"references\",)\n180: DEFAULT_RESOURCE = \"references/obsidian-cli-commands.md\"\n181: # Fallback-only: DEFAULT_RESOURCE is a defer-time suggestion, never unioned\n182: # into a route's loaded set. Scored routes load exactly RESOURCE_MAP[intent];\n183: # zero-score routes load nothing and ask for disambiguation instead.\n184: DEFAULT_RESOURCE_SEMANTICS = \"fallback-only\"\n185: \n186: UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n187:     \"Confirm whether the request is for headless notesmd-cli, the app-backed obsidian CLI, the cyanheads MCP, a plugin, install/setup, or troubleshooting\",\n188:     \"Provide the note name, vault path, command, error text, or target plugin\",\n189:     \"Confirm whether an Obsidian desktop app is running and whether Local REST API + OBSIDIAN_API_KEY are configured\",\n190:     \"Confirm the verification command before completing any write action\",\n191: ]\n192: \n193: INTENT_SIGNALS = {\n194:     \"NOTES_CLI\": {\n195:         \"weight\": 5,\n196:         \"keywords\": [\"note\", \"notes\", \"open\", \"daily\", \"daily note\", \"search\",\n197:                      \"search-content\", \"search content\", \"list\", \"print\", \"create\",\n198:                      \"move\", \"rename\", \"delete\", \"frontmatter\", \"vault\", \"add-vault\",\n199:                      \"remove-vault\", \"list-vaults\", \"set-default-vault\", \"default vault\",\n200:                      \"new note\", \"find note\", \"jot\", \"capture\", \"markdown note\"],\n201:     },\n202:     \"MCP_ADVANCED\": {\n203:         \"weight\": 5,\n204:         \"keywords\": [\"get_note\", \"write_note\", \"search_notes\", \"manage_tags\",\n205:                      \"delete_note\", \"manage tags\", \"add a tag\", \"remove a tag\",\n206:                      \"semantic search\", \"global search\", \"live app\", \"rest api note\",\n207:                      \"structured note\", \"read note via mcp\", \"write note via mcp\"],\n208:     },\n209:     \"PLUGIN_FINANCE\": {\n210:         \"weight\": 5,\n211:         \"keywords\": [\"beancount\", \"beancount finance\", \"beancount-finance\", \"ledger\",\n212:                      \"double-entry\", \"bql\", \"bean-query\", \"bean-price\", \"net worth\",\n213:                      \"transaction\"],\n214:     },\n215:     \"PLUGIN_TABLES\": {\n216:         \"weight\": 5,\n217:         \"keywords\": [\"obsidian tables\", \"obsidian-tables\", \".table.md\", \"table plugin\",\n218:                      \"agentable\", \"columns\", \"rows\", \"formula column\"],\n219:     },\n220:     \"PLUGIN_BRAT\": {\n221:         \"weight\": 5,\n222:         \"keywords\": [\"brat\", \"obsidian42\", \"obsidian42-brat\", \"beta plugin\",\n223:                      \"community plugin install\", \"install plugin from github\", \"frozen version\",\n224:                      \"beta theme\"],\n225:     },\n226:     \"PLUGIN_ICONIC\": {\n227:         \"weight\": 5,\n228:         \"keywords\": [\"iconic\", \"iconic rulebook\", \"icon rules\", \"icon automation\",\n229:                      \"file icons\", \"folder icons\", \"icon color\", \"iconic data json\",\n230:                      \"iconic ruleset\"],\n231:     },\n232:     \"PLUGIN_CHARTS\": {\n233:         \"weight\": 5,\n234:         \"keywords\": [\"charts\", \"chart\", \"obsidian charts\", \"render block\", \"chart block\",\n235:                      \"bar chart\", \"line chart\", \"pie chart\", \"chart json\", \"advanced-chart\"],\n236:     },\n237:     \"PLUGIN_DATAVIEW\": {\n238:         \"weight\": 5,\n239:         \"keywords\": [\"dataview\", \"dql\", \"dataviewjs\", \"inline field\", \"metadata query\",\n240:                      \"frontmatter query\", \"task query\", \"list query\", \"table query\", \"dataview query\"],\n241:     },\n242:     \"PLUGIN_EXCALIDRAW\": {\n243:         \"weight\": 5,\n244:         \"keywords\": [\"excalidraw\", \"drawing\", \"excalidraw.md\", \"drawing note\",\n245:                      \"embedded drawing\", \"whiteboard\", \"excalidraw automate\", \"drawing script\"],\n246:     },\n247:     \"PLUGIN_GIT\": {\n248:         \"weight\": 5,\n249:         \"keywords\": [\"obsidian git\", \"obsidian-git\", \"git plugin\", \"auto backup\",\n250:                      \"vault git\", \"commit vault\", \"push vault\", \"pull vault\", \"git status\", \"git log\"],\n251:     },\n252:     \"PLUGIN_OUTLINER\": {\n253:         \"weight\": 5,\n254:         \"keywords\": [\"outliner\", \"obsidian outliner\", \"list editing\", \"list zoom\",\n255:                      \"outline plugin\", \"fold list\", \"list indentation\"],\n256:     },\n257:     \"PLUGIN_MINIMAL\": {\n258:         \"weight\": 5,\n259:         \"keywords\": [\"minimal\", \"minimal theme\", \"theme\", \"css theme\", \"appearance\",\n260:                      \"theme snippet\", \"style settings\", \"snippets\"],\n261:     },\n262:     \"PLUGIN_HEALTH\": {\n263:         \"weight\": 5,\n264:         \"keywords\": [\"health-md\", \"health.md\", \"health data\", \"apple health\",\n265:                      \"android health\", \"health chart\", \"health visualization\",\n266:                      \"healthkit\", \"health export\", \"healthmd\"],\n267:     },\n268:     \"PLUGINS\": {\n269:         \"weight\": 5,\n270:         \"keywords\": [\"plugin\", \"plugin automation\", \"community plugin\"],\n271:     },\n272:     \"INSTALL\": {\n273:         \"weight\": 6,\n274:         \"keywords\": [\"install notesmd-cli\", \"install obsidian\", \"setup\", \"not found\",\n275:                      \"not installed\", \"api key\", \"api token\", \"local rest api\",\n276:                      \"register cli\", \"enable cli\", \"brew install\", \"scoop install\",\n277:                      \"add-vault\", \"getting started\", \"onboarding\", \"configure\",\n278:                      \"configuration\", \"mcp config\", \"obsidian_base_url\", \"how do i install\"],\n279:     },\n280:     \"TROUBLESHOOT\": {\n281:         \"weight\": 6,\n282:         \"keywords\": [\"error\", \"failed\", \"not working\", \"401\", \"403\", \"404\", \"slow\",\n283:                      \"timeout\", \"empty\", \"no notes\", \"broken\", \"doesn't work\",\n284:                      \"isn't working\", \"won't load\", \"stuck\", \"unauthorized\",\n285:                      \"forbidden\", \"connection refused\", \"can't connect\",\n286:                      \"connection failed\", \"cert\", \"ssl\", \"vault not found\",\n287:                      \"no default vault\"],\n288:     },\n289: }\n290: \n291: # NOTE: no \"DEFAULT\" entry — route_obsidian_resources() never indexes RESOURCE_MAP\n292: # by that key. The selected `intent` is one of the sixteen INTENT_SIGNALS keys above.\n293: # Specific plugin intents always supersede generic PLUGINS whenever any specific signal matches: the highest specific score wins, a tie between specific intents disambiguates, and generic PLUGINS is considered only when no specific plugin signal matches.\n294: # The no-match case is owned by DEFAULT_RESOURCE, whose declared\n295: # fallback-only semantics mean it is SUGGESTED beside the disambiguation checklist,\n296: # never loaded — so obsidian-cli-commands.md can never leak into the MCP_ADVANCED /\n297: # PLUGINS / INSTALL / TROUBLESHOOT routes.\n298: RESOURCE_MAP = {\n299:     \"NOTES_CLI\":     [\"references/obsidian-cli-commands.md\"],\n300:     \"MCP_ADVANCED\":  [\"references/mcp-tools.md\"],\n301:     \"PLUGIN_FINANCE\": [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n302:                        \"references/plugins/beancount-finance/beancount-finance.md\",\n303:                        \"references/plugins/beancount-finance/data-model.md\",\n304:                        \"references/plugins/beancount-finance/workflows.md\",\n305:                        \"references/plugins/beancount-finance/troubleshooting.md\"],\n306:     \"PLUGIN_TABLES\":  [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n307:                        \"references/plugins/obsidian-tables/obsidian-tables.md\",\n308:                        \"references/plugins/obsidian-tables/data-model.md\",\n309:                        \"references/plugins/obsidian-tables/workflows.md\",\n310:                        \"references/plugins/obsidian-tables/troubleshooting.md\"],\n311:     \"PLUGIN_BRAT\":    [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n312:                        \"references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/obsidian42-brat.md\",\n313:                        \"references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/data-model.md\",\n314:                        \"references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/workflows.md\",\n315:                        \"references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/troubleshooting.md\"],\n316:     \"PLUGIN_ICONIC\":  [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n317:                        \"references/plugins/iconic/iconic.md\",\n318:                        \"references/plugins/iconic/data-model.md\",\n319:                        \"references/plugins/iconic/workflows.md\",\n320:                        \"references/plugins/iconic/troubleshooting.md\"],\n321:     \"PLUGIN_CHARTS\":   [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n322:                        \"references/plugins/charts/charts.md\",\n323:                        \"references/plugins/charts/data-model.md\",\n324:                        \"references/plugins/charts/workflows.md\",\n325:                        \"references/plugins/charts/troubleshooting.md\"],\n326:     \"PLUGIN_DATAVIEW\": [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n327:                        \"references/plugins/dataview/dataview.md\",\n328:                        \"references/plugins/dataview/data-model.md\",\n329:                        \"references/plugins/dataview/workflows.md\",\n330:                        \"references/plugins/dataview/troubleshooting.md\"],\n331:     \"PLUGIN_EXCALIDRAW\": [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n332:                        \"references/plugins/excalidraw/excalidraw.md\",\n333:                        \"references/plugins/excalidraw/data-model.md\",\n334:                        \"references/plugins/excalidraw/workflows.md\",\n335:                        \"references/plugins/excalidraw/troubleshooting.md\"],\n336:     \"PLUGIN_GIT\":     [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n337:                        \"references/plugins/git/git.md\",\n338:                        \"references/plugins/git/data-model.md\",\n339:                        \"references/plugins/git/workflows.md\",\n340:                        \"references/plugins/git/troubleshooting.md\"],\n341:     \"PLUGIN_OUTLINER\": [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n342:                        \"references/plugins/outliner/outliner.md\",\n343:                        \"references/plugins/outliner/data-model.md\",\n344:                        \"references/plugins/outliner/workflows.md\",\n345:                        \"references/plugins/outliner/troubleshooting.md\"],\n346:     \"PLUGIN_MINIMAL\": [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n347:                        \"references/plugins/minimal/minimal.md\",\n348:                        \"references/plugins/minimal/data-model.md\",\n349:                        \"references/plugins/minimal/workflows.md\",\n350:                        \"references/plugins/minimal/troubleshooting.md\"],\n351:     \"PLUGIN_HEALTH\":  [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n352:                        \"references/plugins/health-md/health-md.md\",\n353:                        \"references/plugins/health-md/data-model.md\",\n354:                        \"references/plugins/health-md/workflows.md\",\n355:                        \"references/plugins/health-md/troubleshooting.md\"],\n356:     \"PLUGINS\":        [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n357:                        \"references/plugins/beancount-finance/beancount-finance.md\",\n358:                        \"references/plugins/obsidian-tables/obsidian-tables.md\",\n359:                        \"references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/obsidian42-brat.md\",\n360:                        \"references/plugins/iconic/iconic.md\",\n361:                        \"references/plugins/health-md/health-md.md\",\n362:                        \"references/plugins/charts/charts.md\",\n363:                        \"references/plugins/dataview/dataview.md\",\n364:                        \"references/plugins/excalidraw/excalidraw.md\",\n365:                        \"references/plugins/git/git.md\",\n366:                        \"references/plugins/outliner/outliner.md\",\n367:                        \"references/plugins/minimal/minimal.md\"],\n368:     \"INSTALL\":       [\"references/troubleshooting.md\"],\n369:     \"TROUBLESHOOT\":  [\"references/troubleshooting.md\"],\n370: }\n371: \n372: def discover_markdown_resources() -> set[str]:\n373:     docs = []\n374:     for base in RESOURCE_BASES:\n375:         if base.exists():\n376:             docs.extend(path for path in base.rglob(\"*.md\") if path.is_file())\n377: \n378:     return {doc.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix() for doc in docs}\n379: \n380: def _guard_in_skill(relative_path: str) -> str:\n381:     resolved = (SKILL_ROOT / relative_path).resolve()\n382:     resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT)\n383:     if resolved.suffix.lower() != \".md\":\n384:         raise ValueError(f\"Only markdown skill resources are routable: {relative_path}\")\n385:     return resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix()\n386: \n387: def load_if_available(relative_path, loaded, seen, inventory) -> None:\n388:     guarded = _guard_in_skill(relative_path)\n389:     if guarded in inventory and guarded not in seen:\n390:         load(guarded)\n391:         loaded.append(guarded)\n392:         seen.add(guarded)\n393: \n394: def route_obsidian_resources(request: str) -> dict:\n395:     \"\"\"Score intent labels and load available Obsidian reference docs.\"\"\"\n396:     inventory = discover_markdown_resources()\n397:     loaded, seen = [], set()\n398:     request_lower = request.lower()\n399: \n400:     scores = {}\n401:     for intent, config in INTENT_SIGNALS.items():\n402:         score = sum(\n403:             config[\"weight\"] for kw in config[\"keywords\"]\n404:             if kw in request_lower\n405:         )\n406:         if score > 0:\n407:             scores[intent] = score\n408: \n409:     if not scores:\n410:         # Fallback-only: nothing is loaded on a zero-score route; the default\n411:         # reference is offered as a suggestion beside the disambiguation ask.\n412:         return {\n413:             \"load_level\": \"UNKNOWN_FALLBACK\",\n414:             \"needs_disambiguation\": True,\n415:             \"disambiguation_checklist\": UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST,\n416:             \"suggested_fallback\": DEFAULT_RESOURCE,\n417:             \"resources\": loaded,\n418:         }\n419: \n420:     # Error/install keywords boost TROUBLESHOOT/INSTALL regardless of other signals.\n421:     if scores.get(\"TROUBLESHOOT\", 0) > 3:\n422:         intent = \"TROUBLESHOOT\"\n423:     elif scores.get(\"INSTALL\", 0) > 4:\n424:         intent = \"INSTALL\"\n425:     else:\n426:         specific_plugin_intents = (\"PLUGIN_FINANCE\", \"PLUGIN_TABLES\", \"PLUGIN_BRAT\", \"PLUGIN_ICONIC\",\n427:                                    \"PLUGIN_CHARTS\", \"PLUGIN_DATAVIEW\", \"PLUGIN_EXCALIDRAW\",\n428:                                    \"PLUGIN_GIT\", \"PLUGIN_OUTLINER\", \"PLUGIN_MINIMAL\", \"PLUGIN_HEALTH\")\n429:         matched_specific_plugin_intents = [\n430:             plugin_intent\n431:             for plugin_intent in specific_plugin_intents\n432:             if scores.get(plugin_intent, 0) > 0\n433:         ]\n434:         if matched_specific_plugin_intents:\n435:             max_specific_score = max(\n436:                 scores[plugin_intent] for plugin_intent in matched_specific_plugin_intents\n437:             )\n438:             top_specific_plugin_intents = [\n439:                 plugin_intent\n440:                 for plugin_intent in matched_specific_plugin_intents\n441:                 if scores[plugin_intent] == max_specific_score\n442:             ]\n443:             if len(top_specific_plugin_intents) > 1:\n444:                 return {\n445:                     \"needs_disambiguation\": True,\n446:                     \"candidate_intents\": top_specific_plugin_intents,\n447:                     \"disambiguation_checklist\": UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST,\n448:                     \"resources\": loaded,\n449:                 }\n450:             intent = top_specific_plugin_intents[0]\n451:         else:\n452:             intent = max(scores, key=scores.get)\n453: \n454:     for resource in RESOURCE_MAP[intent]:\n455:         load_if_available(resource, loaded, seen, inventory)\n456: \n457:     if not loaded:\n458:         return {\n459:             \"load_level\": \"UNKNOWN_FALLBACK\",\n460:             \"notice\": f\"No Obsidian reference docs available for intent '{intent}'\",\n461:             \"disambiguation_checklist\": UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST,\n462:             \"suggested_fallback\": DEFAULT_RESOURCE,\n463:             \"resources\": loaded,\n464:         }\n465: \n466:     return {\"intent\": intent, \"resources\": loaded}\n467: ```\n468: \n469: ---\n470: \n471: ## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n472: \n473: ### Surface Comparison\n474: \n475: | Dimension | Headless CLI (`notesmd-cli`) | App-backed CLI (`obsidian`) | Cyanheads MCP |\n476: |---|---|---|---|\n477: | **Activation** | `notesmd-cli <command>` in Bash | `obsidian <target>` in Bash | Code Mode `call_tool_chain()` |\n478: | **Running app** | Not required — filesystem only | Required (launches it if not running) | Required + Local REST API |\n479: | **Best for** | Daily note ops anywhere | In-app open / URI actions | Structured reads/writes, tags, search |\n480: | **Auth** | None — reads the vault directory | None — controls the local app | `OBSIDIAN_API_KEY` bearer token |\n481: | **Install** | `brew install yakitrak/yakitrak/notesmd-cli` | Ships with Obsidian desktop v1.12.4+ | `npx -y obsidian-mcp-server@latest` |\n482: | **Config store** | `~/.config/obsidian/obsidian.json` | In-app: Settings → Command line interface | `.utcp_config.json` manual `obsidian` |\n483: | **Output** | Human-readable text | Launches app UI | Structured JSON |\n484: \n485: ### Headless CLI — `notesmd-cli` (Default Path)\n486: \n487: Yakitrak's `notesmd-cli` (binary `notesmd-cli`, renamed from \"obsidian-cli\" to avoid confusion with the official one) operates directly on the vault filesystem, so it works with **no running app**.\n488: \n489: **Step 1: Verify installation**\n490: ```bash\n491: notesmd-cli --version\n492: notesmd-cli list-vaults        # Shows registered vaults + default\n493: ```\n494: \n495: **Step 2: Install if missing**\n496: ```bash\n497: bash .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-obsidian/scripts/install.sh\n498: # or directly:\n499: brew tap yakitrak/yakitrak && brew install yakitrak/yakitrak/notesmd-cli\n500: ```\n501: \n502: **Step 3: Register a vault (one-time)**\n503: ```bash\n504: notesmd-cli add-vault \"/path/to/Vault\"    # writes ~/.config/obsidian/obsidian.json\n505: notesmd-cli set-default-vault \"Vault\"\n506: ```\n507: \n508: **Step 4: Daily note operations**\n509: ```bash\n510: notesmd-cli list                          # List notes in the default vault\n511: notesmd-cli search \"meeting\"              # Search by note name\n512: notesmd-cli search-content \"action item\" # Full-text content search\n513: notesmd-cli print \"Inbox\"                # Print a note to stdout\n514: notesmd-cli create \"New Idea\"            # Create a note\n515: notesmd-cli daily                        # Open/append today's daily note\n516: ```\n517: \n518: ### App-backed CLI — official `obsidian` (Live-App Path)\n519: \n520: The official `obsidian` CLI shipped GA in Obsidian desktop **v1.12.4** (Feb 2026). It is a **remote control for a running app** (it launches the app if not running), not a headless tool. There is no npm/brew package — it ships with the desktop app.\n521: \n522: **Enable in-app:** Settings → General → Command line interface → toggle on → \"Register CLI\" (auto-adds `obsidian` to PATH on macOS/Linux). Use it for in-app opens and `obsidian://` URI actions when a live app is the target.\n523: \n524: ### Cyanheads MCP — `obsidian-mcp-server` (Structured Path)\n525: \n526: The default MCP is cyanheads' `obsidian-mcp-server` (npm **@3.2.9**), launched over **stdio** via `npx -y obsidian-mcp-server@latest` (it also supports http on `127.0.0.1:3010/mcp`). It talks to the vault through the **Local REST API plugin v4.0.0+**, so it needs a **running Obsidian + the plugin enabled + an API key**.\n527: \n528: **Prerequisites:**\n529: - Code Mode MCP configured, with the `obsidian` manual in `.utcp_config.json` (not `opencode.json`, that file is for native/non-Code-Mode MCP tools)\n530: - Obsidian running with the Local REST API plugin enabled and an API key generated\n531: - `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_API_KEY` (required), `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL` (default `http://127.0.0.1:27123`), `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_SSL` (default `false`) available to Code Mode\n532: \n533: **Configuration** (`.utcp_config.json`, `manual_call_templates`):\n534: ```json\n535: {\n536:   \"name\": \"obsidian\",\n537:   \"call_template_type\": \"mcp\",\n538:   \"config\": {\n539:     \"mcpServers\": {\n540:       \"obsidian\": {\n541:         \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n542:         \"command\": \"npx\",\n543:         \"args\": [\"-y\", \"obsidian-mcp-server@latest\"],\n544:         \"env\": {\n545:           \"OBSIDIAN_API_KEY\": \"${obsidian_OBSIDIAN_API_KEY}\",\n546:           \"OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL\": \"${obsidian_OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL}\",\n547:           \"OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_SSL\": \"${obsidian_OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_SSL}\"\n548:         }\n549:       }\n550:     }\n551:   }\n552: }\n553: ```\n554: \n555: The `obsidian_` env prefix matches the manual name `obsidian`, so `${obsidian_OBSIDIAN_API_KEY}` resolves correctly. This registration is already in place: the `obsidian` manual lives in `.utcp_config.json` and the `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_*` keys in `.env.example`. This skill documents that wiring; it does not rewrite those files.\n556: \n557: **Tools:** the server exposes **14 `obsidian_*` tools**. The core five are `obsidian_get_note`, `obsidian_write_note`, `obsidian_search_notes`, `obsidian_manage_tags`, `obsidian_delete_note`; the full 14-tool catalog with per-tool inputs lives in `references/mcp-tools.md`. Confirm every name with `tool_info()`/`list_tools()` before calling — never guess it from a description.\n558: \n559: **Invocation via Code Mode** (`call_tool_chain` takes a single `code` string):\n560: ```typescript\n561: // Tool naming: obsidian.obsidian_{tool_name}\n562: const result = await call_tool_chain({\n563:   code: `\n564:     const note = await obsidian.obsidian_get_note({ path: \"Inbox/Idea.md\" });\n565:     return note;\n566:   `,\n567: });\n568: ```\n569: \n570: **When to prefer the MCP:**\n571: - Structured note reads/writes where you need JSON back, not terminal text\n572: - Tag management (`obsidian_manage_tags`) across a live vault\n573: - Global or semantic search over an active, plugin-backed vault\n574: \n575: **Limitations:**\n576: - Requires a running Obsidian + Local REST API plugin + API key (headless CLI has none of these needs)\n577: - Requires Code Mode MCP to be configured\n578: - `OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_SSL` defaults to `false`; only enable it behind a trusted TLS endpoint\n579: \n580: **Alternative MCP servers (two exist — do not conflate the tool names):** (1) **Local REST API's own built-in MCP** — the `obsidian-local-rest-api` plugin (v5.1.0+) serves a Streamable HTTP MCP at `https://127.0.0.1:27124/mcp/` exposing **16 `vault_*` tools** (`vault_read`/`vault_write`/`vault_patch`/`search_simple`/`tag_list`/…) — validated working, needs no extra npm package, and is a DIFFERENT surface from the cyanheads `obsidian_*` tools. (2) StevenStavrakis' `obsidian-mcp` (npm @1.0.6) is filesystem-based — treat its no-app/no-token claim as `VERIFY`.\n581: \n582: ---\n583: \n584: ## 4. RULES\n585: \n586: ### ✅ ALWAYS\n587: \n588: 1. **Resolve the execution profile before acting** — headless `notesmd-cli` is the default; only route to the app-backed `obsidian` CLI or the MCP when a live app (and, for the MCP, Local REST API + `OBSIDIAN_API_KEY`) is actually available. Probe, do not assume.\n589: 2. **Register and confirm the vault first** — run `notesmd-cli list-vaults` and, if empty, `notesmd-cli add-vault <path>` + `set-default-vault <name>` before any note operation.\n590: 3. **Preview destructive note ops** — for `move` and `delete`, confirm the exact note name with `notesmd-cli list` / `search` before running the write; deletions are hard to reverse.\n591: 4. **Quote note names and paths** — note titles and vault paths contain spaces; always wrap them in quotes in Bash.\n592: 5. **Run `notesmd-cli --version` (and, for the MCP path, confirm the Local REST API is reachable) as preflight** before starting an Obsidian session.\n593: 6. **Treat empty `notesmd-cli list` / `search` results as valid** — an empty vault or no-match search is not an error. Verify the default vault and query spelling before escalating.\n594: 7. **Confirm MCP tool names with `tool_info()`** before calling `obsidian.obsidian_*` — the callable form is `obsidian.obsidian_{tool_name}`.\n595: \n596: ### ⛔ NEVER\n597: \n598: 1. **Never assume a running app for the default path** — `notesmd-cli` is filesystem-only and needs no app; do not launch Obsidian just to run a headless note op.\n599: 2. **Never confuse the two CLIs** — `notesmd-cli` (Yakitrak, headless) and `obsidian` (official, app-backed) are different binaries with different behavior. The official one requires and controls a running app.\n600: 3. **Never use the StevenStavrakis `obsidian-mcp` as the default MCP** — this skill's MCP path is the cyanheads `obsidian-mcp-server`. The Stavrakis server is only the documented headless alternative.\n601: 4. **Never auto-modify `.utcp_config.json`, `.env.example`, `opencode.json`, or hub files** — the `obsidian` manual is already registered there; this skill only documents it. If the wiring ever needs changing, print the config for the user; never write these files programmatically.\n602: 5. **Never hardcode the API key or base URL in commands or notes** — read them from `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_API_KEY` / `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL` in the Code Mode environment.\n603: 6. **Never fabricate notes** — if `notesmd-cli list`/`search` returns empty, the vault or query is genuinely empty. Report it clearly.\n604: 7. **Never enable `OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_SSL` blindly** — it defaults to `false`; only turn it on behind a trusted TLS endpoint.\n605: \n606: ### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n607: \n608: - `notesmd-cli` is not installed and `scripts/install.sh` fails → report the OS/package-manager (brew/scoop/AUR) and Go toolchain state\n609: - `notesmd-cli list-vaults` shows no vault or no default → direct to `add-vault` + `set-default-vault`\n610: - The MCP connection fails → verify the `obsidian` manual in `.utcp_config.json` launches `npx -y obsidian-mcp-server@latest` over stdio, that Obsidian is running with Local REST API v4.0.0+ enabled, and that `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_API_KEY` / `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL` are set\n611: - A `401`/`403` from the MCP → the API key is missing, wrong, or the Local REST API plugin is disabled\n612: - A connection-refused / SSL error on `OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL` → the plugin is not listening on the expected port, or `OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_SSL` is mismatched with the endpoint\n613: \n614: ---\n615: \n616: ## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n617: \n618: - [ ] `notesmd-cli --version` prints a version string\n619: - [ ] `notesmd-cli list-vaults` shows at least one registered vault with a default\n620: - [ ] `notesmd-cli list` returns notes for the default vault (empty list is valid)\n621: - [ ] `notesmd-cli search-content \"<query>\"` returns body matches (title `search` is broken in v0.3.6 — use `list` + filter for names)\n622: - [ ] For in-app work: `obsidian \"<vault/path>\"` opens the note in the running app\n623: - [ ] For MCP work: a Code Mode `obsidian.obsidian_get_note` call returns note content as JSON\n624: \n625: ---\n626: \n627: ## 6. INTEGRATION POINTS\n628: \n629: **Gate 2 (Skill Routing):** This skill activates at ≥0.8 confidence for Obsidian note/vault requests. The skill advisor matches on: `obsidian`, `notesmd-cli`, `obsidian vault`, `note management`, `markdown notes`, `local rest api`.\n630: \n631: **Code Mode MCP:** The cyanheads MCP tools are invoked via `mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain`. Tool naming convention: `obsidian.obsidian_{tool_name}`. See `references/mcp-tools.md` for the full 14-tool catalog.\n632: \n633: **Memory:** Save Obsidian workflow context (default vault name, base URL, active plugin set) using `/memory:save` when switching sessions.\n634: \n635: **Tool Usage:** Use Bash for `notesmd-cli` and the official `obsidian` CLI. Use `mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain` for cyanheads MCP operations. Use Read to load references on demand.\n636: \n637: ---\n638: \n639: ## 7. QUICK REFERENCE\n640: \n641: ### notesmd-cli Command Cheat Sheet (headless)\n642: \n643: | Category | Command | Description |\n644: |---|---|---|\n645: | **Vaults** | `notesmd-cli add-vault \"<path>\"` | Register a vault |\n646: | | `notesmd-cli remove-vault \"<name>\"` | Unregister a vault |\n647: | | `notesmd-cli list-vaults` | List registered vaults + default |\n648: | | `notesmd-cli set-default-vault \"<name>\"` | Set the default vault |\n649: | **Read** | `notesmd-cli list` | List notes in the default vault |\n650: | | `notesmd-cli search \"<query>\"` | Search by note name |\n651: | | `notesmd-cli search-content \"<query>\"` | Full-text content search |\n652: | | `notesmd-cli print \"<name>\"` | Print a note to stdout |\n653: | **Write** | `notesmd-cli create \"<name>\"` | Create a note |\n654: | | `notesmd-cli daily` | Open/append today's daily note |\n655: | | `notesmd-cli move \"<a>\" \"<b>\"` | Move / rename a note |\n656: | | `notesmd-cli delete \"<name>\"` | Delete a note |\n657: | | `notesmd-cli frontmatter \"<name>\"` | Edit a note's frontmatter |\n658: | **Open** | `notesmd-cli open \"<name>\"` | Open a note |\n659: \n660: ### Official `obsidian` CLI (app-backed)\n661: \n662: | Command | Description |\n663: |---|---|\n664: | `obsidian \"<vault/path>\"` | Open a note in the running desktop app (launches it if needed) |\n665: | `obsidian \"obsidian://...\"` | Trigger an `obsidian://` URI action in the live app |\n666: \n667: *(Enable first: Settings → General → Command line interface → Register CLI. Ships with Obsidian desktop v1.12.4+.)*\n668: \n669: ### Cyanheads MCP Call Pattern (Code Mode)\n670: \n671: ```typescript\n672: // Tool naming: obsidian.obsidian_{tool_name}  — 14 tools total\n673: await call_tool_chain({\n674:   code: `\n675:     const hit  = await obsidian.obsidian_search_notes({ query: \"roadmap\" });\n676:     const note = await obsidian.obsidian_get_note({ path: hit[0].path });\n677:     await obsidian.obsidian_manage_tags({ path: hit[0].path, add: [\"reviewed\"] });\n678:     return note;\n679:   `,\n680: });\n681: ```\n682: \n683: ---\n684: \n685: ## 8. REFERENCES AND RELATED RESOURCES\n686: \n687: **Reference Files (load on demand via router):**\n688: - `references/obsidian-cli-commands.md` — Full `notesmd-cli` + official `obsidian` CLI command reference with agent patterns\n689: - `references/mcp-tools.md` — Cyanheads `obsidian-mcp-server` 14-tool catalog, priorities, and `call_tool_chain()` invocation\n690: - `references/troubleshooting.md` — Install, vault, auth, Local REST API and MCP failures\n691: - `references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md` — How plugin-driven note automation is operated\n692: - `references/plugins/beancount-finance/beancount-finance.md` — Beancount Ledger / beancount-finance plugin index\n693: - `references/plugins/beancount-finance/data-model.md` — Beancount Ledger settings, layout, directives, and BQL data model\n694: - `references/plugins/beancount-finance/workflows.md` — Beancount Ledger file-layer recipes\n695: - `references/plugins/beancount-finance/troubleshooting.md` — Beancount Ledger failure and recovery recipes\n696: - `references/plugins/obsidian-tables/obsidian-tables.md` — Obsidian Tables plugin index\n697: - `references/plugins/obsidian-tables/data-model.md` — `.table.md` envelope, columns, rows, formulas, and views\n698: - `references/plugins/obsidian-tables/workflows.md` — Obsidian Tables file-layer recipes\n699: - `references/plugins/obsidian-tables/troubleshooting.md` — Obsidian Tables failure and recovery recipes\n700: - `references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/obsidian42-brat.md` — BRAT beta-plugin install/update index\n701: - `references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/data-model.md` — BRAT `data.json` and release-policy data model\n702: - `references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/workflows.md` — BRAT stage, register, activate, and update recipes\n703: - `references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/troubleshooting.md` — BRAT release, asset, compatibility, and path recovery recipes\n704: - `references/plugins/iconic/iconic.md` — Iconic icon/color rulebook plugin index (usage companion: `assets/plugins/iconic/iconic-rules.full.md`; canonical full rule payload: `assets/plugins/iconic/iconic-rules.full.json`, 21 file + 11 folder rules)\n705: - `references/plugins/iconic/data-model.md` — Iconic `data.json` keys, rule schema, and the merge-only rulebook contract\n706: - `references/plugins/iconic/workflows.md` — Iconic file-layer recipes: add/edit/disable rules, flip toggles, apply the canonical rulebook\n707: - `references/plugins/iconic/troubleshooting.md` — Iconic failure and recovery recipes\n708: \n709: Install guide (front door): [INSTALL-GUIDE.md](INSTALL-GUIDE.md) — condensed top-level install doc for both CLI profiles and the MCP; `references/troubleshooting.md` is the router's INSTALL/TROUBLESHOOT-intent target.\n710: \n711: **Scripts:**\n712: - `scripts/install.sh` — Installs `notesmd-cli` and prints the MCP config snippet\n713: - `scripts/doctor.sh` — Diagnoses the CLI + MCP setup\n714: \n715: **Embedded Servers:**\n716: - `mcp-servers/obsidian-cli/README.md` — `notesmd-cli` install pointer (brew/scoop/AUR/source); run `setup.sh`\n717: - `mcp-servers/obsidian-mcp/README.md` — Cyanheads `obsidian-mcp-server` configuration notes (stdio via `npx -y obsidian-mcp-server@latest`, `OBSIDIAN_API_KEY`/`OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL`/`OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_SSL`)\n718: \n719: **Examples:**\n720: - `examples/README.md` — Guide to the example note-workflow scripts\n721: \n722: **Related Skills:**\n723: - `mcp-click-up` — Structural sibling; same two-path (CLI + MCP) orchestrator pattern\n724: - `mcp-code-mode` — Code Mode MCP orchestration (used for cyanheads MCP invocation)\n725: \n726: **External:**\n727: - notesmd-cli repository: https://github.com/Yakitrak/obsidian-cli\n728: - cyanheads obsidian-mcp-server: https://github.com/cyanheads/obsidian-mcp-server\n729: - Obsidian Local REST API plugin: https://github.com/coddingtonbear/obsidian-local-rest-api\n\n(End of file - total 729 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\nname: mcp-obsidian\ndescription: Makes AI use inside Obsidian effective: vault and note operations across the headless notesmd-cli, the app-backed official obsidian CLI, and the cyanheads MCP, plus deep plugin and theme knowledge (Beancount, Tables, BRAT, Health.md, Iconic, Charts, Dataview, Excalidraw, Git, Outliner, Minimal) operated at the file layer. Embedded install and agent safety invariants.\nallowed-tools: [Bash, Edit, Glob, Grep, mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain, Read, Write]\nversion: 0.18.0.0\n---\n\n<!-- keywords: obsidian, obsidian vault, notesmd-cli, obsidian-mcp, note management, markdown notes, beancount, local rest api, health-md, health data, iconic, icon rules, iconic rulebook, icon automation, file icons, folder icons, iconic data json, iconic ruleset, iconic-rules.full.json, iconic-rules.full.md, data.json, charts, chart render block, dataview, dql, dataviewjs, inline field, excalidraw, excalidraw.md, drawing note, obsidian-git, vault git, auto backup, outliner, list editing, minimal theme, css theme, theme snippet -->\n\n# mcp-obsidian Skill\n\nThe skill that makes AI use inside Obsidian effective. It operates notes and vaults through three surfaces (headless `notesmd-cli`, the app-backed official `obsidian` CLI, and the cyanheads MCP) and knows the eleven plugin and theme file formats at the file layer, so an agent can read, write, search, and extend what the vault contains without guessing.\n\n---\n\n## 1. WHEN TO USE\n\n### Activation Triggers (explicit user phrases)\n\n- \"obsidian\", \"obsidian vault\", \"notesmd-cli\", \"obsidian-mcp\", \"mcp-obsidian\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-obsidian/SKILL.md","text":"---\nname: mcp-obsidian\ndescription: Makes AI use inside Obsidian effective: vault and note operations across the headless notesmd-cli, the app-backed official obsidian CLI, and the cyanheads MCP, plus deep plugin and theme knowledge (Beancount, Tables, BRAT, Health.md, Iconic, Charts, Dataview, Excalidraw, Git, Outliner, Minimal) operated at the file layer. Embedded install and agent safety invariants.\nallowed-tools: [Bash, Edit, Glob, Grep, mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain, Read, Write]\nversion: 0.18.0.0\n---\n\n<!-- keywords: obsidian, obsidian vault, notesmd-cli, obsidian-mcp, note management, markdown notes, beancount, local rest api, health-md, health data, iconic, icon rules, iconic rulebook, icon automation, file icons, folder icons, iconic data json, iconic ruleset, iconic-rules.full.json, iconic-rules.full.md, data.json, charts, chart render block, dataview, dql, dataviewjs, inline field, excalidraw, excalidraw.md, drawing note, obsidian-git, vault git, auto backup, outliner, list editing, minimal theme, css theme, theme snippet -->\n\n# mcp-obsidian Skill\n\nThe skill that makes AI use inside Obsidian effective. It operates notes and vaults through three surfaces (headless `notesmd-cli`, the app-backed official `obsidian` CLI, and the cyanheads MCP) and knows the eleven plugin and theme file formats at the file layer, so an agent can read, write, search, and extend what the vault contains without guessing.\n\n---\n\n## 1. WHEN TO USE\n\n### Activation Triggers (explicit user phrases)\n\n- \"obsidian\", \"obsidian vault\", \"notesmd-cli\", \"obsidian-mcp\", \"mcp-obsidian\"\n- \"note\", \"notes\", \"markdown note\", \"daily note\", \"vault\"\n- \"create a note\", \"open a note\", \"search notes\", \"search my vault\"\n- \"add a tag to a note\", \"manage frontmatter\", \"delete a note\", \"move a note\"\n- \"obsidian plugin\", \"beancount\", \"beancount finance\", \"obsidian tables\", \"brat\"\n- \"health\", \"health data\", \"apple health\", \"health chart\", \"health-md\", \"health.md\"\n- \"iconic\", \"icons\", \"icon color\", \"file icons\", \"folder icons\", \"icon rules\", \"iconic rulebook\", \"iconic ruleset\", \"iconic data json\", \"icon automation\"\n- \"local rest api\", \"obsidian api key\"\n\n### Automatic Triggers (keyword patterns)\n\n- `notesmd-cli` or `obsidian` (the CLI binary) appears in the request\n- `obsidian` + any action verb (create, open, search, list, print, move, delete, tag)\n- \"vault\" in a note-management context\n- \"daily note\" or \"note frontmatter\" in a personal-knowledge context\n- MCP tool names: `obsidian_get_note`, `obsidian_write_note`, `obsidian_search_notes`\n\n### When NOT to Use\n\n- **StevenStavrakis `obsidian-mcp`** — a different (filesystem-based) MCP server; this skill's MCP path uses the cyanheads `obsidian-mcp-server`. The Stavrakis server is documented only as the headless MCP alternative.\n- Generic markdown authoring with no Obsidian vault — use `@markdown` / `sk-doc`.\n- Non-Obsidian note apps (Notion, Bear, Apple Notes) — wrong surface.\n- Editing arbitrary repo files that merely happen to be markdown — use `Read`/`Edit` directly.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SMART ROUTING\n\n### Resource Loading Levels\n\n```\nALWAYS:    SKILL.md (this file)\nON_DEMAND: references/obsidian-cli-commands.md          (notesmd-cli + official obsidian CLI command details)\n           references/mcp-tools.md                      (cyanheads MCP tool catalog + invocation)\n           references/troubleshooting.md                (error, auth, REST API, or install issue detected)\n           Plugin operation logic:\n             references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md (plugin-driven note automation)\n           Beancount Finance:\n             references/plugins/beancount-finance/beancount-finance.md      (plugin index)\n             references/plugins/beancount-finance/data-model.md\n             references/plugins/beancount-finance/workflows.md\n             references/plugins/beancount-finance/troubleshooting.md\n           Obsidian Tables:\n             references/plugins/obsidian-tables/obsidian-tables.md         (plugin index)\n             references/plugins/obsidian-tables/data-model.md\n             references/plugins/obsidian-tables/workflows.md\n             references/plugins/obsidian-tables/troubleshooting.md\n           Obsidian42 BRAT:\n             references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/obsidian42-brat.md         (plugin index)\n             references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/data-model.md\n             references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/workflows.md\n             references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/troubleshooting.md\n           Health.md Visualizations:\n             references/plugins/health-md/health-md.md                   (plugin index)\n             references/plugins/health-md/data-model.md\n             references/plugins/health-md/workflows.md\n             references/plugins/health-md/troubleshooting.md\n           Iconic:\n             references/plugins/iconic/iconic.md                         (plugin index)\n             references/plugins/iconic/data-model.md\n             references/plugins/iconic/workflows.md\n             references/plugins/iconic/troubleshooting.md\n           Charts:\n             references/plugins/charts/charts.md                         (plugin index)\n             references/plugins/charts/data-model.md\n             references/plugins/charts/workflows.md\n             references/plugins/charts/troubleshooting.md\n           Dataview:\n             references/plugins/dataview/dataview.md                     (plugin index)\n             references/plugins/dataview/data-model.md\n             references/plugins/dataview/workflows.md\n             references/plugins/dataview/troubleshooting.md\n           Excalidraw:\n             references/plugins/excalidraw/excalidraw.md                 (plugin index)\n             references/plugins/excalidraw/data-model.md\n             references/plugins/excalidraw/workflows.md\n             references/plugins/excalidraw/troubleshooting.md\n           Obsidian Git:\n             references/plugins/git/git.md                               (plugin index)\n             references/plugins/git/data-model.md\n             references/plugins/git/workflows.md\n             references/plugins/git/troubleshooting.md\n           Outliner:\n             references/plugins/outliner/outliner.md                     (plugin index)\n             references/plugins/outliner/data-model.md\n             references/plugins/outliner/workflows.md\n             references/plugins/outliner/troubleshooting.md\n           Minimal (theme):\n             references/plugins/minimal/minimal.md                       (plugin index)\n             references/plugins/minimal/data-model.md\n             references/plugins/minimal/workflows.md\n             references/plugins/minimal/troubleshooting.md\n```\n\n### Two Decisions This Router Makes\n\n1. **CLI vs MCP** — filesystem/terminal work goes to a CLI; live-app note reads/writes/tags/search go to the MCP.\n2. **Which CLI profile** — headless `notesmd-cli` (default, no running app) vs the app-backed official `obsidian` CLI (a remote control for a running desktop app).\n\n### Execution Profile Selection\n\n| Surface | Binary / transport | Needs a running app? | Best for |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Headless CLI** | `notesmd-cli` (Bash) | No — operates on the vault filesystem | Daily note ops anywhere: open, daily, search, create, list, print, move, delete, frontmatter, vault management |\n| **App-backed CLI** | `obsidian` (Bash) | Yes — launches/controls the desktop app | In-app actions: opening notes in the live UI, `obsidian://` URI actions, app-context commands |\n| **MCP** | `obsidian.obsidian_*` via Code Mode | Yes — plus Local REST API + `OBSIDIAN_API_KEY` | Structured note reads/writes, tag management, semantic/global search over a live vault |\n\n```python\ndef resolve_execution_profile(request, runtime):\n    \"\"\"Pick the execution surface for an Obsidian operation.\n\n    Best-effort runtime probes — never fabricated:\n      runtime.app_running   -> an Obsidian desktop app is live\n      runtime.rest_api_up   -> Local REST API plugin reachable on OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL\n      runtime.api_key       -> OBSIDIAN_API_KEY present in the Code Mode environment\n    \"\"\"\n    # MCP path needs a live app + Local REST API + token. It is the only surface\n    # for structured note reads/writes, tag management and global/semantic search.\n    if wants_structured_note_ops(request) and runtime.app_running \\\n            and runtime.rest_api_up and runtime.api_key:\n        return \"MCP\"            # cyanheads obsidian-mcp-server via Code Mode\n\n    # The official obsidian CLI is a remote control for a RUNNING app; use it only\n    # for in-app actions (open in UI, obsidian:// URIs) when the app is up.\n    if runtime.app_running and needs_app_command(request):\n        return \"OBSIDIAN_CLI\"   # official `obsidian` CLI\n\n    # Default: headless, filesystem-only, works with no running app or token.\n    return \"NOTESMD_CLI\"        # Yakitrak notesmd-cli\n```\n\n### Operation-to-Tool Routing Table\n\n| Operation | Primary Surface | Command / Tool | Alternative |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Open a note | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli open \"<name>\"` | `obsidian` CLI (in live app) |\n| Open/append daily note | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli daily` | MCP `obsidian_write_note` |\n| Search by note name | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli list` + filter (`search` title-lookup is broken in v0.3.6) | MCP `obsidian_search_notes` |\n| Search note contents | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli search-content \"<query>\"` | MCP `obsidian_search_notes` |\n| List notes | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli list` | MCP `obsidian_search_notes` |\n| Print a note to stdout | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli print \"<name>\"` | MCP `obsidian_get_note` |\n| Create a note | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli create \"<name>\"` | MCP `obsidian_write_note` |\n| Move / rename a note | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli move \"<a>\" \"<b>\"` | n/a |\n| Delete a note | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli delete \"<name>\"` | MCP `obsidian_delete_note` |\n| Edit frontmatter | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli frontmatter \"<name>\"` | MCP `obsidian_manage_tags` |\n| Vault registration | notesmd-cli | `notesmd-cli add-vault` / `set-default-vault` | n/a |\n| **Structured note read** | **MCP** | `obsidian_get_note` | notesmd-cli `print` |\n| **Structured note write** | **MCP** | `obsidian_write_note` | notesmd-cli `create` |\n| **Tag management** | **MCP** | `obsidian_manage_tags` | notesmd-cli `frontmatter` |\n| **Global / semantic search** | **MCP** | `obsidian_search_notes` | notesmd-cli `search-content` |\n| **In-app open / URI action** | **obsidian CLI** | `obsidian \"<vault/path>\"` | n/a |\n| **Plugin-driven automation** | reference | `references/plugins/*` | n/a |\n\n### Smart Router Pseudocode\n\n```python\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSKILL_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nRESOURCE_BASES = (SKILL_ROOT / \"references\",)\nDEFAULT_RESOURCE = \"references/obsidian-cli-commands.md\"\n# Fallback-only: DEFAULT_RESOURCE is a defer-time suggestion, never unioned\n# into a route's loaded set. Scored routes load exactly RESOURCE_MAP[intent];\n# zero-score routes load nothing and ask for disambiguation instead.\nDEFAULT_RESOURCE_SEMANTICS = \"fallback-only\"\n\nUNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n    \"Confirm whether the request is for headless notesmd-cli, the app-backed obsidian CLI, the cyanheads MCP, a plugin, install/setup, or troubleshooting\",\n    \"Provide the note name, vault path, command, error text, or target plugin\",\n    \"Confirm whether an Obsidian desktop app is running and whether Local REST API + OBSIDIAN_API_KEY are configured\",\n    \"Confirm the verification command before completing any write action\",\n]\n\nINTENT_SIGNALS = {\n    \"NOTES_CLI\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"note\", \"notes\", \"open\", \"daily\", \"daily note\", \"search\",\n                     \"search-content\", \"search content\", \"list\", \"print\", \"create\",\n                     \"move\", \"rename\", \"delete\", \"frontmatter\", \"vault\", \"add-vault\",\n                     \"remove-vault\", \"list-vaults\", \"set-default-vault\", \"default vault\",\n                     \"new note\", \"find note\", \"jot\", \"capture\", \"markdown note\"],\n    },\n    \"MCP_ADVANCED\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"get_note\", \"write_note\", \"search_notes\", \"manage_tags\",\n                     \"delete_note\", \"manage tags\", \"add a tag\", \"remove a tag\",\n                     \"semantic search\", \"global search\", \"live app\", \"rest api note\",\n                     \"structured note\", \"read note via mcp\", \"write note via mcp\"],\n    },\n    \"PLUGIN_FINANCE\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"beancount\", \"beancount finance\", \"beancount-finance\", \"ledger\",\n                     \"double-entry\", \"bql\", \"bean-query\", \"bean-price\", \"net worth\",\n                     \"transaction\"],\n    },\n    \"PLUGIN_TABLES\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"obsidian tables\", \"obsidian-tables\", \".table.md\", \"table plugin\",\n                     \"agentable\", \"columns\", \"rows\", \"formula column\"],\n    },\n    \"PLUGIN_BRAT\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"brat\", \"obsidian42\", \"obsidian42-brat\", \"beta plugin\",\n                     \"community plugin install\", \"install plugin from github\", \"frozen version\",\n                     \"beta theme\"],\n    },\n    \"PLUGIN_ICONIC\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"iconic\", \"iconic rulebook\", \"icon rules\", \"icon automation\",\n                     \"file icons\", \"folder icons\", \"icon color\", \"iconic data json\",\n                     \"iconic ruleset\"],\n    },\n    \"PLUGIN_CHARTS\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"charts\", \"chart\", \"obsidian charts\", \"render block\", \"chart block\",\n                     \"bar chart\", \"line chart\", \"pie chart\", \"chart json\", \"advanced-chart\"],\n    },\n    \"PLUGIN_DATAVIEW\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"dataview\", \"dql\", \"dataviewjs\", \"inline field\", \"metadata query\",\n                     \"frontmatter query\", \"task query\", \"list query\", \"table query\", \"dataview query\"],\n    },\n    \"PLUGIN_EXCALIDRAW\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"excalidraw\", \"drawing\", \"excalidraw.md\", \"drawing note\",\n                     \"embedded drawing\", \"whiteboard\", \"excalidraw automate\", \"drawing script\"],\n    },\n    \"PLUGIN_GIT\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"obsidian git\", \"obsidian-git\", \"git plugin\", \"auto backup\",\n                     \"vault git\", \"commit vault\", \"push vault\", \"pull vault\", \"git status\", \"git log\"],\n    },\n    \"PLUGIN_OUTLINER\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"outliner\", \"obsidian outliner\", \"list editing\", \"list zoom\",\n                     \"outline plugin\", \"fold list\", \"list indentation\"],\n    },\n    \"PLUGIN_MINIMAL\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"minimal\", \"minimal theme\", \"theme\", \"css theme\", \"appearance\",\n                     \"theme snippet\", \"style settings\", \"snippets\"],\n    },\n    \"PLUGIN_HEALTH\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"health-md\", \"health.md\", \"health data\", \"apple health\",\n                     \"android health\", \"health chart\", \"health visualization\",\n                     \"healthkit\", \"health export\", \"healthmd\"],\n    },\n    \"PLUGINS\": {\n        \"weight\": 5,\n        \"keywords\": [\"plugin\", \"plugin automation\", \"community plugin\"],\n    },\n    \"INSTALL\": {\n        \"weight\": 6,\n        \"keywords\": [\"install notesmd-cli\", \"install obsidian\", \"setup\", \"not found\",\n                     \"not installed\", \"api key\", \"api token\", \"local rest api\",\n                     \"register cli\", \"enable cli\", \"brew install\", \"scoop install\",\n                     \"add-vault\", \"getting started\", \"onboarding\", \"configure\",\n                     \"configuration\", \"mcp config\", \"obsidian_base_url\", \"how do i install\"],\n    },\n    \"TROUBLESHOOT\": {\n        \"weight\": 6,\n        \"keywords\": [\"error\", \"failed\", \"not working\", \"401\", \"403\", \"404\", \"slow\",\n                     \"timeout\", \"empty\", \"no notes\", \"broken\", \"doesn't work\",\n                     \"isn't working\", \"won't load\", \"stuck\", \"unauthorized\",\n                     \"forbidden\", \"connection refused\", \"can't connect\",\n                     \"connection failed\", \"cert\", \"ssl\", \"vault not found\",\n                     \"no default vault\"],\n    },\n}\n\n# NOTE: no \"DEFAULT\" entry — route_obsidian_resources() never indexes RESOURCE_MAP\n# by that key. The selected `intent` is one of the sixteen INTENT_SIGNALS keys above.\n# Specific plugin intents always supersede generic PLUGINS whenever any specific signal matches: the highest specific score wins, a tie between specific intents disambiguates, and generic PLUGINS is considered only when no specific plugin signal matches.\n# The no-match case is owned by DEFAULT_RESOURCE, whose declared\n# fallback-only semantics mean it is SUGGESTED beside the disambiguation checklist,\n# never loaded — so obsidian-cli-commands.md can never leak into the MCP_ADVANCED /\n# PLUGINS / INSTALL / TROUBLESHOOT routes.\nRESOURCE_MAP = {\n    \"NOTES_CLI\":     [\"references/obsidian-cli-commands.md\"],\n    \"MCP_ADVANCED\":  [\"references/mcp-tools.md\"],\n    \"PLUGIN_FINANCE\": [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/beancount-finance/beancount-finance.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/beancount-finance/data-model.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/beancount-finance/workflows.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/beancount-finance/troubleshooting.md\"],\n    \"PLUGIN_TABLES\":  [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/obsidian-tables/obsidian-tables.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/obsidian-tables/data-model.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/obsidian-tables/workflows.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/obsidian-tables/troubleshooting.md\"],\n    \"PLUGIN_BRAT\":    [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/obsidian42-brat.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/data-model.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/workflows.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/troubleshooting.md\"],\n    \"PLUGIN_ICONIC\":  [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/iconic/iconic.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/iconic/data-model.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/iconic/workflows.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/iconic/troubleshooting.md\"],\n    \"PLUGIN_CHARTS\":   [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/charts/charts.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/charts/data-model.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/charts/workflows.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/charts/troubleshooting.md\"],\n    \"PLUGIN_DATAVIEW\": [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/dataview/dataview.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/dataview/data-model.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/dataview/workflows.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/dataview/troubleshooting.md\"],\n    \"PLUGIN_EXCALIDRAW\": [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/excalidraw/excalidraw.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/excalidraw/data-model.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/excalidraw/workflows.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/excalidraw/troubleshooting.md\"],\n    \"PLUGIN_GIT\":     [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/git/git.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/git/data-model.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/git/workflows.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/git/troubleshooting.md\"],\n    \"PLUGIN_OUTLINER\": [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/outliner/outliner.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/outliner/data-model.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/outliner/workflows.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/outliner/troubleshooting.md\"],\n    \"PLUGIN_MINIMAL\": [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/minimal/minimal.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/minimal/data-model.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/minimal/workflows.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/minimal/troubleshooting.md\"],\n    \"PLUGIN_HEALTH\":  [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/health-md/health-md.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/health-md/data-model.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/health-md/workflows.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/health-md/troubleshooting.md\"],\n    \"PLUGINS\":        [\"references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/beancount-finance/beancount-finance.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/obsidian-tables/obsidian-tables.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/obsidian42-brat.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/iconic/iconic.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/health-md/health-md.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/charts/charts.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/dataview/dataview.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/excalidraw/excalidraw.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/git/git.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/outliner/outliner.md\",\n                       \"references/plugins/minimal/minimal.md\"],\n    \"INSTALL\":       [\"references/troubleshooting.md\"],\n    \"TROUBLESHOOT\":  [\"references/troubleshooting.md\"],\n}\n\ndef discover_markdown_resources() -> set[str]:\n    docs = []\n    for base in RESOURCE_BASES:\n        if base.exists():\n            docs.extend(path for path in base.rglob(\"*.md\") if path.is_file())\n\n    return {doc.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix() for doc in docs}\n\ndef _guard_in_skill(relative_path: str) -> str:\n    resolved = (SKILL_ROOT / relative_path).resolve()\n    resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT)\n    if resolved.suffix.lower() != \".md\":\n        raise ValueError(f\"Only markdown skill resources are routable: {relative_path}\")\n    return resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix()\n\ndef load_if_available(relative_path, loaded, seen, inventory) -> None:\n    guarded = _guard_in_skill(relative_path)\n    if guarded in inventory and guarded not in seen:\n        load(guarded)\n        loaded.append(guarded)\n        seen.add(guarded)\n\ndef route_obsidian_resources(request: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Score intent labels and load available Obsidian reference docs.\"\"\"\n    inventory = discover_markdown_resources()\n    loaded, seen = [], set()\n    request_lower = request.lower()\n\n    scores = {}\n    for intent, config in INTENT_SIGNALS.items():\n        score = sum(\n            config[\"weight\"] for kw in config[\"keywords\"]\n            if kw in request_lower\n        )\n        if score > 0:\n            scores[intent] = score\n\n    if not scores:\n        # Fallback-only: nothing is loaded on a zero-score route; the default\n        # reference is offered as a suggestion beside the disambiguation ask.\n        return {\n            \"load_level\": \"UNKNOWN_FALLBACK\",\n            \"needs_disambiguation\": True,\n            \"disambiguation_checklist\": UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST,\n            \"suggested_fallback\": DEFAULT_RESOURCE,\n            \"resources\": loaded,\n        }\n\n    # Error/install keywords boost TROUBLESHOOT/INSTALL regardless of other signals.\n    if scores.get(\"TROUBLESHOOT\", 0) > 3:\n        intent = \"TROUBLESHOOT\"\n    elif scores.get(\"INSTALL\", 0) > 4:\n        intent = \"INSTALL\"\n    else:\n        specific_plugin_intents = (\"PLUGIN_FINANCE\", \"PLUGIN_TABLES\", \"PLUGIN_BRAT\", \"PLUGIN_ICONIC\",\n                                   \"PLUGIN_CHARTS\", \"PLUGIN_DATAVIEW\", \"PLUGIN_EXCALIDRAW\",\n                                   \"PLUGIN_GIT\", \"PLUGIN_OUTLINER\", \"PLUGIN_MINIMAL\", \"PLUGIN_HEALTH\")\n        matched_specific_plugin_intents = [\n            plugin_intent\n            for plugin_intent in specific_plugin_intents\n            if scores.get(plugin_intent, 0) > 0\n        ]\n        if matched_specific_plugin_intents:\n            max_specific_score = max(\n                scores[plugin_intent] for plugin_intent in matched_specific_plugin_intents\n            )\n            top_specific_plugin_intents = [\n                plugin_intent\n                for plugin_intent in matched_specific_plugin_intents\n                if scores[plugin_intent] == max_specific_score\n            ]\n            if len(top_specific_plugin_intents) > 1:\n                return {\n                    \"needs_disambiguation\": True,\n                    \"candidate_intents\": top_specific_plugin_intents,\n                    \"disambiguation_checklist\": UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST,\n                    \"resources\": loaded,\n                }\n            intent = top_specific_plugin_intents[0]\n        else:\n            intent = max(scores, key=scores.get)\n\n    for resource in RESOURCE_MAP[intent]:\n        load_if_available(resource, loaded, seen, inventory)\n\n    if not loaded:\n        return {\n            \"load_level\": \"UNKNOWN_FALLBACK\",\n            \"notice\": f\"No Obsidian reference docs available for intent '{intent}'\",\n            \"disambiguation_checklist\": UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST,\n            \"suggested_fallback\": DEFAULT_RESOURCE,\n            \"resources\": loaded,\n        }\n\n    return {\"intent\": intent, \"resources\": loaded}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Surface Comparison\n\n| Dimension | Headless CLI (`notesmd-cli`) | App-backed CLI (`obsidian`) | Cyanheads MCP |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Activation** | `notesmd-cli <command>` in Bash | `obsidian <target>` in Bash | Code Mode `call_tool_chain()` |\n| **Running app** | Not required — filesystem only | Required (launches it if not running) | Required + Local REST API |\n| **Best for** | Daily note ops anywhere | In-app open / URI actions | Structured reads/writes, tags, search |\n| **Auth** | None — reads the vault directory | None — controls the local app | `OBSIDIAN_API_KEY` bearer token |\n| **Install** | `brew install yakitrak/yakitrak/notesmd-cli` | Ships with Obsidian desktop v1.12.4+ | `npx -y obsidian-mcp-server@latest` |\n| **Config store** | `~/.config/obsidian/obsidian.json` | In-app: Settings → Command line interface | `.utcp_config.json` manual `obsidian` |\n| **Output** | Human-readable text | Launches app UI | Structured JSON |\n\n### Headless CLI — `notesmd-cli` (Default Path)\n\nYakitrak's `notesmd-cli` (binary `notesmd-cli`, renamed from \"obsidian-cli\" to avoid confusion with the official one) operates directly on the vault filesystem, so it works with **no running app**.\n\n**Step 1: Verify installation**\n```bash\nnotesmd-cli --version\nnotesmd-cli list-vaults        # Shows registered vaults + default\n```\n\n**Step 2: Install if missing**\n```bash\nbash .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-obsidian/scripts/install.sh\n# or directly:\nbrew tap yakitrak/yakitrak && brew install yakitrak/yakitrak/notesmd-cli\n```\n\n**Step 3: Register a vault (one-time)**\n```bash\nnotesmd-cli add-vault \"/path/to/Vault\"    # writes ~/.config/obsidian/obsidian.json\nnotesmd-cli set-default-vault \"Vault\"\n```\n\n**Step 4: Daily note operations**\n```bash\nnotesmd-cli list                          # List notes in the default vault\nnotesmd-cli search \"meeting\"              # Search by note name\nnotesmd-cli search-content \"action item\" # Full-text content search\nnotesmd-cli print \"Inbox\"                # Print a note to stdout\nnotesmd-cli create \"New Idea\"            # Create a note\nnotesmd-cli daily                        # Open/append today's daily note\n```\n\n### App-backed CLI — official `obsidian` (Live-App Path)\n\nThe official `obsidian` CLI shipped GA in Obsidian desktop **v1.12.4** (Feb 2026). It is a **remote control for a running app** (it launches the app if not running), not a headless tool. There is no npm/brew package — it ships with the desktop app.\n\n**Enable in-app:** Settings → General → Command line interface → toggle on → \"Register CLI\" (auto-adds `obsidian` to PATH on macOS/Linux). Use it for in-app opens and `obsidian://` URI actions when a live app is the target.\n\n### Cyanheads MCP — `obsidian-mcp-server` (Structured Path)\n\nThe default MCP is cyanheads' `obsidian-mcp-server` (npm **@3.2.9**), launched over **stdio** via `npx -y obsidian-mcp-server@latest` (it also supports http on `127.0.0.1:3010/mcp`). It talks to the vault through the **Local REST API plugin v4.0.0+**, so it needs a **running Obsidian + the plugin enabled + an API key**.\n\n**Prerequisites:**\n- Code Mode MCP configured, with the `obsidian` manual in `.utcp_config.json` (not `opencode.json`, that file is for native/non-Code-Mode MCP tools)\n- Obsidian running with the Local REST API plugin enabled and an API key generated\n- `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_API_KEY` (required), `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL` (default `http://127.0.0.1:27123`), `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_SSL` (default `false`) available to Code Mode\n\n**Configuration** (`.utcp_config.json`, `manual_call_templates`):\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"obsidian\",\n  \"call_template_type\": \"mcp\",\n  \"config\": {\n    \"mcpServers\": {\n      \"obsidian\": {\n        \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n        \"command\": \"npx\",\n        \"args\": [\"-y\", \"obsidian-mcp-server@latest\"],\n        \"env\": {\n          \"OBSIDIAN_API_KEY\": \"${obsidian_OBSIDIAN_API_KEY}\",\n          \"OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL\": \"${obsidian_OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL}\",\n          \"OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_SSL\": \"${obsidian_OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_SSL}\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe `obsidian_` env prefix matches the manual name `obsidian`, so `${obsidian_OBSIDIAN_API_KEY}` resolves correctly. This registration is already in place: the `obsidian` manual lives in `.utcp_config.json` and the `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_*` keys in `.env.example`. This skill documents that wiring; it does not rewrite those files.\n\n**Tools:** the server exposes **14 `obsidian_*` tools**. The core five are `obsidian_get_note`, `obsidian_write_note`, `obsidian_search_notes`, `obsidian_manage_tags`, `obsidian_delete_note`; the full 14-tool catalog with per-tool inputs lives in `references/mcp-tools.md`. Confirm every name with `tool_info()`/`list_tools()` before calling — never guess it from a description.\n\n**Invocation via Code Mode** (`call_tool_chain` takes a single `code` string):\n```typescript\n// Tool naming: obsidian.obsidian_{tool_name}\nconst result = await call_tool_chain({\n  code: `\n    const note = await obsidian.obsidian_get_note({ path: \"Inbox/Idea.md\" });\n    return note;\n  `,\n});\n```\n\n**When to prefer the MCP:**\n- Structured note reads/writes where you need JSON back, not terminal text\n- Tag management (`obsidian_manage_tags`) across a live vault\n- Global or semantic search over an active, plugin-backed vault\n\n**Limitations:**\n- Requires a running Obsidian + Local REST API plugin + API key (headless CLI has none of these needs)\n- Requires Code Mode MCP to be configured\n- `OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_SSL` defaults to `false`; only enable it behind a trusted TLS endpoint\n\n**Alternative MCP servers (two exist — do not conflate the tool names):** (1) **Local REST API's own built-in MCP** — the `obsidian-local-rest-api` plugin (v5.1.0+) serves a Streamable HTTP MCP at `https://127.0.0.1:27124/mcp/` exposing **16 `vault_*` tools** (`vault_read`/`vault_write`/`vault_patch`/`search_simple`/`tag_list`/…) — validated working, needs no extra npm package, and is a DIFFERENT surface from the cyanheads `obsidian_*` tools. (2) StevenStavrakis' `obsidian-mcp` (npm @1.0.6) is filesystem-based — treat its no-app/no-token claim as `VERIFY`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. RULES\n\n### ✅ ALWAYS\n\n1. **Resolve the execution profile before acting** — headless `notesmd-cli` is the default; only route to the app-backed `obsidian` CLI or the MCP when a live app (and, for the MCP, Local REST API + `OBSIDIAN_API_KEY`) is actually available. Probe, do not assume.\n2. **Register and confirm the vault first** — run `notesmd-cli list-vaults` and, if empty, `notesmd-cli add-vault <path>` + `set-default-vault <name>` before any note operation.\n3. **Preview destructive note ops** — for `move` and `delete`, confirm the exact note name with `notesmd-cli list` / `search` before running the write; deletions are hard to reverse.\n4. **Quote note names and paths** — note titles and vault paths contain spaces; always wrap them in quotes in Bash.\n5. **Run `notesmd-cli --version` (and, for the MCP path, confirm the Local REST API is reachable) as preflight** before starting an Obsidian session.\n6. **Treat empty `notesmd-cli list` / `search` results as valid** — an empty vault or no-match search is not an error. Verify the default vault and query spelling before escalating.\n7. **Confirm MCP tool names with `tool_info()`** before calling `obsidian.obsidian_*` — the callable form is `obsidian.obsidian_{tool_name}`.\n\n### ⛔ NEVER\n\n1. **Never assume a running app for the default path** — `notesmd-cli` is filesystem-only and needs no app; do not launch Obsidian just to run a headless note op.\n2. **Never confuse the two CLIs** — `notesmd-cli` (Yakitrak, headless) and `obsidian` (official, app-backed) are different binaries with different behavior. The official one requires and controls a running app.\n3. **Never use the StevenStavrakis `obsidian-mcp` as the default MCP** — this skill's MCP path is the cyanheads `obsidian-mcp-server`. The Stavrakis server is only the documented headless alternative.\n4. **Never auto-modify `.utcp_config.json`, `.env.example`, `opencode.json`, or hub files** — the `obsidian` manual is already registered there; this skill only documents it. If the wiring ever needs changing, print the config for the user; never write these files programmatically.\n5. **Never hardcode the API key or base URL in commands or notes** — read them from `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_API_KEY` / `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL` in the Code Mode environment.\n6. **Never fabricate notes** — if `notesmd-cli list`/`search` returns empty, the vault or query is genuinely empty. Report it clearly.\n7. **Never enable `OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_SSL` blindly** — it defaults to `false`; only turn it on behind a trusted TLS endpoint.\n\n### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n\n- `notesmd-cli` is not installed and `scripts/install.sh` fails → report the OS/package-manager (brew/scoop/AUR) and Go toolchain state\n- `notesmd-cli list-vaults` shows no vault or no default → direct to `add-vault` + `set-default-vault`\n- The MCP connection fails → verify the `obsidian` manual in `.utcp_config.json` launches `npx -y obsidian-mcp-server@latest` over stdio, that Obsidian is running with Local REST API v4.0.0+ enabled, and that `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_API_KEY` / `obsidian_OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL` are set\n- A `401`/`403` from the MCP → the API key is missing, wrong, or the Local REST API plugin is disabled\n- A connection-refused / SSL error on `OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL` → the plugin is not listening on the expected port, or `OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_SSL` is mismatched with the endpoint\n\n---\n\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- [ ] `notesmd-cli --version` prints a version string\n- [ ] `notesmd-cli list-vaults` shows at least one registered vault with a default\n- [ ] `notesmd-cli list` returns notes for the default vault (empty list is valid)\n- [ ] `notesmd-cli search-content \"<query>\"` returns body matches (title `search` is broken in v0.3.6 — use `list` + filter for names)\n- [ ] For in-app work: `obsidian \"<vault/path>\"` opens the note in the running app\n- [ ] For MCP work: a Code Mode `obsidian.obsidian_get_note` call returns note content as JSON\n\n---\n\n## 6. INTEGRATION POINTS\n\n**Gate 2 (Skill Routing):** This skill activates at ≥0.8 confidence for Obsidian note/vault requests. The skill advisor matches on: `obsidian`, `notesmd-cli`, `obsidian vault`, `note management`, `markdown notes`, `local rest api`.\n\n**Code Mode MCP:** The cyanheads MCP tools are invoked via `mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain`. Tool naming convention: `obsidian.obsidian_{tool_name}`. See `references/mcp-tools.md` for the full 14-tool catalog.\n\n**Memory:** Save Obsidian workflow context (default vault name, base URL, active plugin set) using `/memory:save` when switching sessions.\n\n**Tool Usage:** Use Bash for `notesmd-cli` and the official `obsidian` CLI. Use `mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain` for cyanheads MCP operations. Use Read to load references on demand.\n\n---\n\n## 7. QUICK REFERENCE\n\n### notesmd-cli Command Cheat Sheet (headless)\n\n| Category | Command | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Vaults** | `notesmd-cli add-vault \"<path>\"` | Register a vault |\n| | `notesmd-cli remove-vault \"<name>\"` | Unregister a vault |\n| | `notesmd-cli list-vaults` | List registered vaults + default |\n| | `notesmd-cli set-default-vault \"<name>\"` | Set the default vault |\n| **Read** | `notesmd-cli list` | List notes in the default vault |\n| | `notesmd-cli search \"<query>\"` | Search by note name |\n| | `notesmd-cli search-content \"<query>\"` | Full-text content search |\n| | `notesmd-cli print \"<name>\"` | Print a note to stdout |\n| **Write** | `notesmd-cli create \"<name>\"` | Create a note |\n| | `notesmd-cli daily` | Open/append today's daily note |\n| | `notesmd-cli move \"<a>\" \"<b>\"` | Move / rename a note |\n| | `notesmd-cli delete \"<name>\"` | Delete a note |\n| | `notesmd-cli frontmatter \"<name>\"` | Edit a note's frontmatter |\n| **Open** | `notesmd-cli open \"<name>\"` | Open a note |\n\n### Official `obsidian` CLI (app-backed)\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `obsidian \"<vault/path>\"` | Open a note in the running desktop app (launches it if needed) |\n| `obsidian \"obsidian://...\"` | Trigger an `obsidian://` URI action in the live app |\n\n*(Enable first: Settings → General → Command line interface → Register CLI. Ships with Obsidian desktop v1.12.4+.)*\n\n### Cyanheads MCP Call Pattern (Code Mode)\n\n```typescript\n// Tool naming: obsidian.obsidian_{tool_name}  — 14 tools total\nawait call_tool_chain({\n  code: `\n    const hit  = await obsidian.obsidian_search_notes({ query: \"roadmap\" });\n    const note = await obsidian.obsidian_get_note({ path: hit[0].path });\n    await obsidian.obsidian_manage_tags({ path: hit[0].path, add: [\"reviewed\"] });\n    return note;\n  `,\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. REFERENCES AND RELATED RESOURCES\n\n**Reference Files (load on demand via router):**\n- `references/obsidian-cli-commands.md` — Full `notesmd-cli` + official `obsidian` CLI command reference with agent patterns\n- `references/mcp-tools.md` — Cyanheads `obsidian-mcp-server` 14-tool catalog, priorities, and `call_tool_chain()` invocation\n- `references/troubleshooting.md` — Install, vault, auth, Local REST API and MCP failures\n- `references/plugins/plugin-operation-logic.md` — How plugin-driven note automation is operated\n- `references/plugins/beancount-finance/beancount-finance.md` — Beancount Ledger / beancount-finance plugin index\n- `references/plugins/beancount-finance/data-model.md` — Beancount Ledger settings, layout, directives, and BQL data model\n- `references/plugins/beancount-finance/workflows.md` — Beancount Ledger file-layer recipes\n- `references/plugins/beancount-finance/troubleshooting.md` — Beancount Ledger failure and recovery recipes\n- `references/plugins/obsidian-tables/obsidian-tables.md` — Obsidian Tables plugin index\n- `references/plugins/obsidian-tables/data-model.md` — `.table.md` envelope, columns, rows, formulas, and views\n- `references/plugins/obsidian-tables/workflows.md` — Obsidian Tables file-layer recipes\n- `references/plugins/obsidian-tables/troubleshooting.md` — Obsidian Tables failure and recovery recipes\n- `references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/obsidian42-brat.md` — BRAT beta-plugin install/update index\n- `references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/data-model.md` — BRAT `data.json` and release-policy data model\n- `references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/workflows.md` — BRAT stage, register, activate, and update recipes\n- `references/plugins/obsidian42-brat/troubleshooting.md` — BRAT release, asset, compatibility, and path recovery recipes\n- `references/plugins/iconic/iconic.md` — Iconic icon/color rulebook plugin index (usage companion: `assets/plugins/iconic/iconic-rules.full.md`; canonical full rule payload: `assets/plugins/iconic/iconic-rules.full.json`, 21 file + 11 folder rules)\n- `references/plugins/iconic/data-model.md` — Iconic `data.json` keys, rule schema, and the merge-only rulebook contract\n- `references/plugins/iconic/workflows.md` — Iconic file-layer recipes: add/edit/disable rules, flip toggles, apply the canonical rulebook\n- `references/plugins/iconic/troubleshooting.md` — Iconic failure and recovery recipes\n\nInstall guide (front door): [INSTALL-GUIDE.md](INSTALL-GUIDE.md) — condensed top-level install doc for both CLI profiles and the MCP; `references/troubleshooting.md` is the router's INSTALL/TROUBLESHOOT-intent target.\n\n**Scripts:**\n- `scripts/install.sh` — Installs `notesmd-cli` and prints the MCP config snippet\n- `scripts/doctor.sh` — Diagnoses the CLI + MCP setup\n\n**Embedded Servers:**\n- `mcp-servers/obsidian-cli/README.md` — `notesmd-cli` install pointer (brew/scoop/AUR/source); run `setup.sh`\n- `mcp-servers/obsidian-mcp/README.md` — Cyanheads `obsidian-mcp-server` configuration notes (stdio via `npx -y obsidian-mcp-server@latest`, `OBSIDIAN_API_KEY`/`OBSIDIAN_BASE_URL`/`OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_SSL`)\n\n**Examples:**\n- `examples/README.md` — Guide to the example note-workflow scripts\n\n**Related Skills:**\n- `mcp-click-up` — Structural sibling; same two-path (CLI + MCP) orchestrator pattern\n- `mcp-code-mode` — Code Mode MCP orchestration (used for cyanheads MCP invocation)\n\n**External:**\n- notesmd-cli repository: https://github.com/Yakitrak/obsidian-cli\n- cyanheads obsidian-mcp-server: https://github.com/cyanheads/obsidian-mcp-server\n- Obsidian Local REST API plugin: https://github.com/coddingtonbear/obsidian-local-rest-api","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":729,"totalLines":729,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-obsidian/SKILL.md","time":{"start":1787344249681,"end":1787344249699}},"id":"prt_02604e0dd001s2C8YPQFvRHwUu","sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","messageID":"msg_02604c4fd0010rqTRjBmfEeEJ3"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787344250562,"sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_0b694f64a6d34a738bf6b9a7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-outputs.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-outputs.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Research Output Files Reference\n3: description: Markdown output structures for strategy, iterations, dashboard, synthesis, and resource-map artifacts.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"research output files\"\n6:   - \"research iteration files\"\n7:   - \"research synthesis document\"\n8:   - \"research resource map\"\n9:   - \"research strategy file\"\n10:   - \"spec anchoring output\"\n11: importance_tier: normal\n12: contextType: implementation\n13: version: 1.14.0.3\n14: ---\n15: \n16: # Deep Research Output Files Reference\n17: \n18: This reference covers human-readable packet outputs. JSONL records live in `state-jsonl.md`; reducer ownership lives in `state-reducer-registry.md`.\n19: \n20: ---\n21: \n22: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n23: \n24: ### Purpose\n25: \n26: Define the human-readable deep-research packet outputs: strategy, iteration markdown, synthesis, dashboard, resource map, and bounded spec anchoring.\n27: \n28: ### When to Use\n29: \n30: Load this reference when writing or validating markdown outputs rather than JSONL records.\n31: \n32: ### Core Principle\n33: \n34: Human-readable outputs must stay synchronized with raw state and respect reducer ownership.\n35: \n36: ---\n37: \n38: ## 2. STRATEGY FILE\n39: \n40: `deep-research-strategy.md` is the persistent research plan. The reducer owns machine-managed sections.\n41: \n42: Required sections:\n43: \n44: - Research Topic\n45: - Known Context\n46: - Key Questions\n47: - Answered Questions\n48: - What Worked\n49: - What Failed\n50: - Exhausted Approaches\n51: - Ruled-Out Directions\n52: - Next Focus\n53: \n54: Update protocol:\n55: \n56: - read strategy before each iteration;\n57: - choose one focus from `Next Focus`;\n58: - append what worked, failed, and was ruled out;\n59: - update answered/open questions through reducer-owned sections;\n60: - when a STOP candidate is blocked, override `Next Focus` with the blocker recovery focus.\n61: \n62: ---\n63: \n64: ## 3. ITERATION FILES\n65: \n66: Iteration files are write-once markdown narratives.\n67: \n68: ```text\n69: research/iterations/iteration-001.md\n70: research/iterations/iteration-002.md\n71: research/iterations/iteration-003.md\n72: ```\n73: \n74: Required shape:\n75: \n76: | Markdown Element | Required Content |\n77: |------------------|------------------|\n78: | H1 title | `Iteration N: Focus Area` |\n79: | `Focus` section | What this iteration investigated |\n80: | `Findings` section | Evidence-backed findings with source citations |\n81: | `Sources Consulted` section | Files, URLs, memory hits, or commands used |\n82: | `Assessment` section | `newInfoRatio`, novelty justification, and confidence notes |\n83: | `Reflection` section | What worked, failed, or was ruled out |\n84: | `Recommended Next Focus` section | One concrete next focus |\n85: \n86: Every finding must cite a source such as `[SOURCE: file:path:line]` or `[SOURCE: https://example.test]`.\n87: \n88: ---\n89: \n90: ## 4. RESEARCH SYNTHESIS\n91: \n92: `research.md` is the workflow-owned synthesis output at `{artifact_dir}/research.md`.\n93: \n94: Rules:\n95: \n96: - progressive synthesis may update the file during the loop;\n97: - final synthesis consolidates duplicate findings and unresolved gaps;\n98: - prior findings are not silently overwritten;\n99: - generated or machine-owned sections must be marked explicitly when the workflow uses them;\n100: - when `resource_map_present` is true, cite `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` in References.\n101: \n102: ---\n103: \n104: ## 5. DASHBOARD\n105: \n106: `deep-research-dashboard.md` is auto-generated from JSONL, strategy, and registry state.\n107: \n108: Expected sections:\n109: \n110: | Section | Source |\n111: |---------|--------|\n112: | Iteration Table | JSONL iteration records |\n113: | Question Status | Strategy + registry |\n114: | Convergence Trend | `convergenceSignals` + reducer |\n115: | Dead Ends | JSONL `ruledOut` + strategy |\n116: | Blocked Stops | Registry blocked-stop history |\n117: | Graph Convergence | Graph convergence registry fields |\n118: | Next Focus | Strategy |\n119: \n120: Generation rules:\n121: \n122: - regenerate after each iteration evaluation;\n123: - compute derived values from raw state;\n124: - overwrite the full dashboard rather than appending;\n125: - if state is missing, write a minimal \"No iteration data available\" dashboard;\n126: - agent writes are discarded on next refresh.\n127: \n128: ---\n129: \n130: ## 6. RESOURCE MAP\n131: \n132: When `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` exists at init:\n133: \n134: - persist `resource_map_present: true` in config;\n135: - summarize section counts and themes into strategy `Known Context`;\n136: - treat listed files as known inventory, not net-new discoveries;\n137: - cite the map in final synthesis references;\n138: - emit `{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md` from converged deltas unless disabled.\n139: \n140: When absent:\n141: \n142: - persist `resource_map_present: false`;\n143: - write `resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate` into `Known Context`;\n144: - continue normally.\n145: \n146: ---\n147: \n148: ## 7. SPEC ANCHORING OUTPUT\n149: \n150: `references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md` defines bounded `spec.md` writes:\n151: \n152: - acquire `research/.deep-research.lock`;\n153: - classify `folder_state`;\n154: - seed or append bounded context during init when allowed;\n155: - replace exactly one generated findings fence during synthesis.\n156: \n157: This output path is protocol-owned, not iteration-agent owned.\n\n(End of file - total 157 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Output Files Reference\ndescription: Markdown output structures for strategy, iterations, dashboard, synthesis, and resource-map artifacts.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"research output files\"\n  - \"research iteration files\"\n  - \"research synthesis document\"\n  - \"research resource map\"\n  - \"research strategy file\"\n  - \"spec anchoring output\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.14.0.3\n---\n\n# Deep Research Output Files Reference\n\nThis reference covers human-readable packet outputs. JSONL records live in `state-jsonl.md`; reducer ownership lives in `state-reducer-registry.md`.\n\n---","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-outputs.md","text":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Output Files Reference\ndescription: Markdown output structures for strategy, iterations, dashboard, synthesis, and resource-map artifacts.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"research output files\"\n  - \"research iteration files\"\n  - \"research synthesis document\"\n  - \"research resource map\"\n  - \"research strategy file\"\n  - \"spec anchoring output\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.14.0.3\n---\n\n# Deep Research Output Files Reference\n\nThis reference covers human-readable packet outputs. JSONL records live in `state-jsonl.md`; reducer ownership lives in `state-reducer-registry.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nDefine the human-readable deep-research packet outputs: strategy, iteration markdown, synthesis, dashboard, resource map, and bounded spec anchoring.\n\n### When to Use\n\nLoad this reference when writing or validating markdown outputs rather than JSONL records.\n\n### Core Principle\n\nHuman-readable outputs must stay synchronized with raw state and respect reducer ownership.\n\n---\n\n## 2. STRATEGY FILE\n\n`deep-research-strategy.md` is the persistent research plan. The reducer owns machine-managed sections.\n\nRequired sections:\n\n- Research Topic\n- Known Context\n- Key Questions\n- Answered Questions\n- What Worked\n- What Failed\n- Exhausted Approaches\n- Ruled-Out Directions\n- Next Focus\n\nUpdate protocol:\n\n- read strategy before each iteration;\n- choose one focus from `Next Focus`;\n- append what worked, failed, and was ruled out;\n- update answered/open questions through reducer-owned sections;\n- when a STOP candidate is blocked, override `Next Focus` with the blocker recovery focus.\n\n---\n\n## 3. ITERATION FILES\n\nIteration files are write-once markdown narratives.\n\n```text\nresearch/iterations/iteration-001.md\nresearch/iterations/iteration-002.md\nresearch/iterations/iteration-003.md\n```\n\nRequired shape:\n\n| Markdown Element | Required Content |\n|------------------|------------------|\n| H1 title | `Iteration N: Focus Area` |\n| `Focus` section | What this iteration investigated |\n| `Findings` section | Evidence-backed findings with source citations |\n| `Sources Consulted` section | Files, URLs, memory hits, or commands used |\n| `Assessment` section | `newInfoRatio`, novelty justification, and confidence notes |\n| `Reflection` section | What worked, failed, or was ruled out |\n| `Recommended Next Focus` section | One concrete next focus |\n\nEvery finding must cite a source such as `[SOURCE: file:path:line]` or `[SOURCE: https://example.test]`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. RESEARCH SYNTHESIS\n\n`research.md` is the workflow-owned synthesis output at `{artifact_dir}/research.md`.\n\nRules:\n\n- progressive synthesis may update the file during the loop;\n- final synthesis consolidates duplicate findings and unresolved gaps;\n- prior findings are not silently overwritten;\n- generated or machine-owned sections must be marked explicitly when the workflow uses them;\n- when `resource_map_present` is true, cite `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` in References.\n\n---\n\n## 5. DASHBOARD\n\n`deep-research-dashboard.md` is auto-generated from JSONL, strategy, and registry state.\n\nExpected sections:\n\n| Section | Source |\n|---------|--------|\n| Iteration Table | JSONL iteration records |\n| Question Status | Strategy + registry |\n| Convergence Trend | `convergenceSignals` + reducer |\n| Dead Ends | JSONL `ruledOut` + strategy |\n| Blocked Stops | Registry blocked-stop history |\n| Graph Convergence | Graph convergence registry fields |\n| Next Focus | Strategy |\n\nGeneration rules:\n\n- regenerate after each iteration evaluation;\n- compute derived values from raw state;\n- overwrite the full dashboard rather than appending;\n- if state is missing, write a minimal \"No iteration data available\" dashboard;\n- agent writes are discarded on next refresh.\n\n---\n\n## 6. RESOURCE MAP\n\nWhen `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` exists at init:\n\n- persist `resource_map_present: true` in config;\n- summarize section counts and themes into strategy `Known Context`;\n- treat listed files as known inventory, not net-new discoveries;\n- cite the map in final synthesis references;\n- emit `{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md` from converged deltas unless disabled.\n\nWhen absent:\n\n- persist `resource_map_present: false`;\n- write `resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate` into `Known Context`;\n- continue normally.\n\n---\n\n## 7. SPEC ANCHORING OUTPUT\n\n`references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md` defines bounded `spec.md` writes:\n\n- acquire `research/.deep-research.lock`;\n- classify `folder_state`;\n- seed or append bounded context during init when allowed;\n- replace exactly one generated findings fence during synthesis.\n\nThis output path is protocol-owned, not iteration-agent owned.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":157,"totalLines":157,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-outputs.md","time":{"start":1787344250551,"end":1787344250559}},"id":"prt_02604e3df0015d3WUK8N0GN2qb","sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","messageID":"msg_02604c4fd0010rqTRjBmfEeEJ3"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787344251508,"sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_57215e4b964840348ec7f78a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Research Strategy Template\n3: description: Runtime template copied to research/ during initialization to track research progress, focus decisions, and outcomes across iterations.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep research strategy\"\n6:   - \"research strategy template\"\n7:   - \"research session tracking\"\n8:   - \"exhausted research approaches\"\n9:   - \"research stop conditions\"\n10:   - \"ruled out research directions\"\n11: importance_tier: normal\n12: contextType: planning\n13: version: 1.14.0.19\n14: ---\n15: \n16: # Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n17: \n18: Runtime template copied to `{spec_folder}/research/` during initialization. Tracks research progress across iterations.\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: ### Purpose\n23: \n24: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep research session. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n25: \n26: ### Usage\n27: \n28: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{spec_folder}/research/deep-research-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Key Questions, Known Context, and Research Boundaries from config and memory context.\n29: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, writes iteration evidence, and the reducer refreshes What Worked/Failed, answered questions, carried-forward questions, ruled-out directions, and Next Focus.\n30: - **Mutability:** Mutable — analyst-owned sections remain stable, while machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration. Section 3 is a generated projection from the reducer registry.\n31: - **Protection:** Shared state with explicit ownership boundaries. Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n32: \n33: ### Question Injection Surface\n34: \n35: Use `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl` to append external questions during an active run. Each line is one JSON object with:\n36: \n37: - `id`: stable inbox record identifier\n38: - `text`: question text to promote\n39: - `source`: concrete source label, such as an angle bank entry, analyst strategy, or operator note\n40: - `origin`: one of `angle-bank`, `analyst-strategy`, `operator`, or `legacy-import`\n41: - `injectedAtIteration`: iteration number when the question was introduced\n42: - `promotedQuestionId`: promoted registry question id, or `null` until promotion\n43: \n44: The reducer reads the inbox on every reduce step and carries `origin` into the question registry and dashboard badges. Direct edits to Section 3 still work as a compatibility path, but they are attributed as `legacy-import`.\n45: \n46: Question ownership is explicit:\n47: \n48: - Inbox rows are immutable input.\n49: - The reducer registry is canonical question state.\n50: - Section 3 is rendered only from the registry view.\n51: \n52: When an inbox row targets an existing registry question but carries different text, the reducer keeps the registry value, records `operatorDecision: needs_decision`, and appends a `question_conflict` event with both `inboxValue` and `registryValue`.\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: ## 2. TOPIC\n57: [Research topic from config -- set during initialization]\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n62: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n63: Generated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\n64: \n65: - [ ] [Question 1 -- identified during initialization or iteration 1]\n66: - [ ] [Question 2]\n67: - [ ] [Question 3]\n68: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n73: [What this research session is NOT trying to answer -- populated during initialization]\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n78: [Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n83: ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n84: [None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n85: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n86: \n87: ---\n88: \n89: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n90: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n91: ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n92: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n93: - [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n94: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n99: ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n100: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n101: - [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n102: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n103: \n104: ---\n105: \n106: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n107: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n108: [Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n109: \n110: ### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n111: - What was tried: [specific approaches attempted]\n112: - Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n113: - Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n114: \n115: ### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n116: - What worked: [successful approaches in this category]\n117: - Prefer for: [related questions where this category may help]\n118: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n119: \n120: ---\n121: \n122: <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n123: ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n124: [Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n125: - [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n126: <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n127: \n128: ---\n129: \n130: <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n131: ## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n132: - Completed pivots: 0\n133: - Failed pivots: 0\n134: - Audited overrides: 0\n135: - Saturated: none yet\n136: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n137: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n138: <!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n139: \n140: ---\n141: \n142: <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n143: ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n144: [Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n145: <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n150: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n151: [Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration]\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n157: ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n158: [Populated during initialization from memory_context() results, if any prior work exists]\n159: \n160: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n161: \n162: Populate during initialization when the target is codebase-scoped. Keep this pointer-based and small:\n163: \n164: - Source pointers: paths, symbols, or resource-map entries relevant to the topic.\n165: - Reuse candidates: existing utilities, patterns, docs, or agents worth extending.\n166: - Integration points: files or contracts the research is likely to touch.\n167: - Constraints and risks: scope limits, stale graph or memory gaps, and known non-goals.\n168: \n169: Do not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use `@context` for one-shot retrieval, and use this snapshot only to seed the research loop.\n170: \n171: ---\n172: \n173: ## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n174: - Max iterations: [from config]\n175: - Convergence threshold: [from config]\n176: - Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n177: - Progressive synthesis: true (default)\n178: - research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n179: - Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\n180: - Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\n181: - Question injection surface: `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`\n182: - Question conflict owner: reducer registry; `question_conflict` events surface inbox/registry disagreements for operator decision\n183: - Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`\n184: - Capability matrix: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\n185: - Capability matrix doc: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md`\n186: - Capability resolver: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`\n187: - Current generation: [from config.lineage.generation]\n188: - Started: [timestamp]\n\n(End of file - total 188 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy Template\ndescription: Runtime template copied to research/ during initialization to track research progress, focus decisions, and outcomes across iterations.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep research strategy\"\n  - \"research strategy template\"\n  - \"research session tracking\"\n  - \"exhausted research approaches\"\n  - \"research stop conditions\"\n  - \"ruled out research directions\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\nversion: 1.14.0.19\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n\nRuntime template copied to `{spec_folder}/research/` during initialization. Tracks research progress across iterations.\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md","text":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy Template\ndescription: Runtime template copied to research/ during initialization to track research progress, focus decisions, and outcomes across iterations.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep research strategy\"\n  - \"research strategy template\"\n  - \"research session tracking\"\n  - \"exhausted research approaches\"\n  - \"research stop conditions\"\n  - \"ruled out research directions\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\nversion: 1.14.0.19\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n\nRuntime template copied to `{spec_folder}/research/` during initialization. Tracks research progress across iterations.\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nServes as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep research session. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n\n### Usage\n\n- **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{spec_folder}/research/deep-research-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Key Questions, Known Context, and Research Boundaries from config and memory context.\n- **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, writes iteration evidence, and the reducer refreshes What Worked/Failed, answered questions, carried-forward questions, ruled-out directions, and Next Focus.\n- **Mutability:** Mutable — analyst-owned sections remain stable, while machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration. Section 3 is a generated projection from the reducer registry.\n- **Protection:** Shared state with explicit ownership boundaries. Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n\n### Question Injection Surface\n\nUse `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl` to append external questions during an active run. Each line is one JSON object with:\n\n- `id`: stable inbox record identifier\n- `text`: question text to promote\n- `source`: concrete source label, such as an angle bank entry, analyst strategy, or operator note\n- `origin`: one of `angle-bank`, `analyst-strategy`, `operator`, or `legacy-import`\n- `injectedAtIteration`: iteration number when the question was introduced\n- `promotedQuestionId`: promoted registry question id, or `null` until promotion\n\nThe reducer reads the inbox on every reduce step and carries `origin` into the question registry and dashboard badges. Direct edits to Section 3 still work as a compatibility path, but they are attributed as `legacy-import`.\n\nQuestion ownership is explicit:\n\n- Inbox rows are immutable input.\n- The reducer registry is canonical question state.\n- Section 3 is rendered only from the registry view.\n\nWhen an inbox row targets an existing registry question but carries different text, the reducer keeps the registry value, records `operatorDecision: needs_decision`, and appends a `question_conflict` event with both `inboxValue` and `registryValue`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n[Research topic from config -- set during initialization]\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\nGenerated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\n\n- [ ] [Question 1 -- identified during initialization or iteration 1]\n- [ ] [Question 2]\n- [ ] [Question 3]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n[What this research session is NOT trying to answer -- populated during initialization]\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n[Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n- [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n- [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n\n### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n- What was tried: [specific approaches attempted]\n- Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n- Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n\n### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n- What worked: [successful approaches in this category]\n- Prefer for: [related questions where this category may help]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n- [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n[Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n[Populated during initialization from memory_context() results, if any prior work exists]\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\nPopulate during initialization when the target is codebase-scoped. Keep this pointer-based and small:\n\n- Source pointers: paths, symbols, or resource-map entries relevant to the topic.\n- Reuse candidates: existing utilities, patterns, docs, or agents worth extending.\n- Integration points: files or contracts the research is likely to touch.\n- Constraints and risks: scope limits, stale graph or memory gaps, and known non-goals.\n\nDo not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use `@context` for one-shot retrieval, and use this snapshot only to seed the research loop.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: [from config]\n- Convergence threshold: [from config]\n- Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true (default)\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\n- Question injection surface: `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`\n- Question conflict owner: reducer registry; `question_conflict` events surface inbox/registry disagreements for operator decision\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`\n- Capability matrix: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\n- Capability matrix doc: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md`\n- Capability resolver: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`\n- Current generation: [from config.lineage.generation]\n- Started: [timestamp]","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":188,"totalLines":188,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md","time":{"start":1787344251499,"end":1787344251507}},"id":"prt_02604e7aa001qarPWc5gzqQCm3","sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","messageID":"msg_02604c4fd0010rqTRjBmfEeEJ3"}}
