atures](https://github.com/security/advanced-security)\n        -   [Copilot for BusinessEnterprise-grade AI features](https://github.com/features/copilot/copilot-business)\n        -   [Premium SupportEnterprise-grade 24/7 support](https://github.com/enterprise/premium-support)\n        \n    \n-   [Pricing](https://github.com/pricing)\n\nSearch/\n\n[Sign in](/login?return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fbgarciamoura%2Fobsidian-notion-bases-plugin)\n\n[Sign up](/signup?ref_cta=Sign+up&ref_loc=header+logged+out&ref_page=%2F%3Cuser-name%3E%2F%3Crepo-name%3E&source=header-repo&source_repo=bgarciamoura%2Fobsidian-notion-bases-plugin)\n\nAppearance settings\n\nYou signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. Dismiss alert\n\n[bgarciamoura](/bgarciamoura) / **[obsidian-notion-bases-plugin](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin)** Public\n\n-   [Notifications](/login?return_to=%2Fbgarciamoura%2Fobsidian-notion-bases-plugin) You must be signed in to change notification settings\n-   [Fork 10](/login?return_to=%2Fbgarciamoura%2Fobsidian-notion-bases-plugin)\n-   [Star 134](/login?return_to=%2Fbgarciamoura%2Fobsidian-notion-bases-plugin)\n    \n\n-   [Code](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin)\n-   [Issues 5](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/issues)\n-   [Pull requests 1](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/pulls)\n-   [Discussions](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/discussions)\n-   [Actions](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/actions)\n-   [Projects](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/projects)\n-   [Security and quality 0](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/security)\n-   [Insights](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/pulse)\n\nAdditional navigation options\n\n-   [Code](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin)\n-   [Issues](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/issues)\n-   [Pull requests](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/pulls)\n-   [Discussions](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/discussions)\n-   [Actions](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/actions)\n-   [Projects](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/projects)\n-   [Security and quality](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/security)\n-   [Insights](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/pulse)\n\n [](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin)\n\nmain\n\n[Branches](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/branches)[Tags](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/tags)\n\n[](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/branches)[](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/tags)\n\nGo to file\n\nCode\n\nOpen more actions menu\n\n## Latest commit\n\n## History\n\n[334 Commits](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/commits/main/)\n\n[](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/commits/main/)334 Commits\n\n## Folders and files\n\nName\n\nName\n\nLast commit message\n\nLast commit date\n\n[.github](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/tree/main/.github \".github\")\n\n[.github](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/tree/main/.github \".github\")\n\n[docs/images](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/tree/main/docs/images \"This path skips through empty directories\")\n\n[docs/images](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/tree/main/docs/images \"This path skips through empty directories\")\n\n[src](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/tree/main/src \"src\")\n\n[src](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/tree/main/src \"src\")\n\n[tests](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/tree/main/tests \"tests\")\n\n[tests](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/tree/main/tests \"tests\")\n\n[.editorconfig](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/.editorconfig \".editorconfig\")\n\n[.editorconfig](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/.editorconfig \".editorconfig\")\n\n[.gitignore](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/.gitignore \".gitignore\")\n\n[.gitignore](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/.gitignore \".gitignore\")\n\n[CODE\\_OF\\_CONDUCT.md](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md \"CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\")\n\n[CODE\\_OF\\_CONDUCT.md](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md \"CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\")\n\n[CONTRIBUTING.md](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md \"CONTRIBUTING.md\")\n\n[CONTRIBUTING.md](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md \"CONTRIBUTING.md\")\n\n[LICENSE](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/LICENSE \"LICENSE\")\n\n[LICENSE](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/LICENSE \"LICENSE\")\n\n[README.md](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/README.md \"README.md\")\n\n[README.md](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/README.md \"README.md\")\n\n[SECURITY.md](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/SECURITY.md \"SECURITY.md\")\n\n[SECURITY.md](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/SECURITY.md \"SECURITY.md\")\n\n[demo-vault.zip](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/demo-vault.zip \"demo-vault.zip\")\n\n[demo-vault.zip](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/demo-vault.zip \"demo-vault.zip\")\n\n[esbuild.config.mjs](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/esbuild.config.mjs \"esbuild.config.mjs\")\n\n[esbuild.config.mjs](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/esbuild.config.mjs \"esbuild.config.mjs\")\n\n[eslint.config.mts](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/eslint.config.mts \"eslint.config.mts\")\n\n[eslint.config.mts](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/eslint.config.mts \"eslint.config.mts\")\n\n[manifest.json](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/manifest.json \"manifest.json\")\n\n[manifest.json](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/manifest.json \"manifest.json\")\n\n[package-lock.json](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/package-lock.json \"package-lock.json\")\n\n[package-lock.json](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/package-lock.json \"package-lock.json\")\n\n[package.json](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/package.json \"package.json\")\n\n[package.json](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/package.json \"package.json\")\n\n[release.mjs](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/release.mjs \"release.mjs\")\n\n[release.mjs](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/release.mjs \"release.mjs\")\n\n[styles.css](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/styles.css \"styles.css\")\n\n[styles.css](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/styles.css \"styles.css\")\n\n[tsconfig.json](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/tsconfig.json \"tsconfig.json\")\n\n[tsconfig.json](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/tsconfig.json \"tsconfig.json\")\n\n[versions.json](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/versions.json \"versions.json\")\n\n[versions.json](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/versions.json \"versions.json\")\n\n[vitest.config.ts](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/vitest.config.ts \"vitest.config.ts\")\n\n[vitest.config.ts](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/vitest.config.ts \"vitest.config.ts\")\n\nView all files\n\n## Repository files navigation\n\n-   [README](#)\n-   [Code of conduct](#)\n-   [Contributing](#)\n-   [GPL-3.0 license](#)\n-   [Security](#)\n\nMore items\n\n# Notion Bases for Obsidian\n\n[](#notion-bases-for-obsidian)\n\n### The database engine Obsidian deserves\n\n[](#the-database-engine-obsidian-deserves)\n\n**7 views. 18 column types. Charts, subtasks, formulas and relations. Zero code required.**\n\nTurn any folder into a Notion-style database with Table, Board (Kanban), Gallery, List, Calendar, Timeline (Gantt), and Chart views — powered by plain Markdown and frontmatter. Your data stays yours, always.\n\n**Now available in Obsidian's Community Plugins directory** — [install it directly in the app](https://obsidian.md/plugins?id=notion-bases)\n\n[![GitHub release](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/66e2369841933f2d03a518edb4b13c7f2289c76dc06b2e8190c7cb0c865673fd/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f6769746875622f762f72656c656173652f626761726369616d6f7572612f6f6273696469616e2d6e6f74696f6e2d62617365732d706c7567696e3f7374796c653d666f722d7468652d626164676526636f6c6f723d376333616564)](https://github.com/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/releases/latest) [![Obsidian](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/201513893e12b76f2ef6ddf82498faeae8e4cdc1ce8655e35f8c5c0fa9ba945f/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f4f6273696469616e2d254532253839254135253230312e382e372d3763336165643f7374796c653d666f722d7468652d6261646765266c6f676f3d6f6273696469616e266c6f676f436f6c6f723d7768697465)](https://obsidian.md) [![License](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/1e88976276d74eb72fb6f1d95d69394684fdf3234ccd73594d9ba76cb38654d9/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f6769746875622f6c6963656e73652f626761726369616d6f7572612f6f6273696469616e2d6e6f74696f6e2d62617365732d706c7567696e3f7374796c653d666f722d7468652d6261646765)](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/LICENSE) [![Downloads](https://camo.githubusercontent.)](https://github.com/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/releases)\n\n[![Stars](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/bbebbe43409deb29d2f9c3b9cbc19fdaf8c6ca41995bcad9f2c62d76e6a5ce2b/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f6769746875622f73746172732f626761726369616d6f7572612f6f6273696469616e2d6e6f74696f6e2d62617365732d706c7567696e3f7374796c653d666f722d7468652d626164676526636f6c6f723d663563353432)](https://github.com/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/stargazers) [![Issues](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/d774daee1fe9098e240cdf185e16672f71a554c87082029903ee4baa80d7d442/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f6769746875622f6973737565732f626761726369616d6f7572612f6f6273696469616e2d6e6f74696f6e2d62617365732d706c7567696e3f7374796c653d666f722d7468652d6261646765)](https://github.com/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/issues) [![PRs Welcome](https://camo.githubusercontent.com/fa591ba514d87a6b179fe081d4c2c28fc9ed531bd1c3362be14f461834126478/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f5052732d77656c636f6d652d627269676874677265656e3f7374796c653d666f722d7468652d6261646765)](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n\n**[Website](https://bgarciamoura.github.io/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/)** · **[Latest Release](https://github.com/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/releases/latest)** · **[Report Bug](https://github.com/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/issues/new?template=bug_report.yml)** · **[Request Feature](https://github.com/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/issues/new?template=feature_request.yml)**\n\n[![Hero — Table view overview](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/raw/main/docs/images/hero.png)](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/docs/images/hero.png)\n\n---\n\n## Highlights\n\n[](#highlights)\n\n-   **7 views** — Table, Board (Kanban), Gallery, List, Calendar, Timeline (Gantt), Chart\n-   **18 column types** — Title, Text, Number, Select, Multi-select, Checkbox, Date, URL, Email, Phone, Status, Formula, Relation, Lookup, Rollup, Image, Audio, Video\n-   **Charts** — Bar, line, and pie charts with configurable axes, aggregations, and smart formatting — pure SVG, zero dependencies\n-   **Subtasks** — Hierarchical rows with expand/collapse, up to 3 levels deep, powered by self-relation columns\n-   **Rollup columns** — Aggregate values across related databases with 7 functions (sum, count, avg, min, max, count\\_values, list)\n-   **Formula engine** — Spreadsheet-style functions: `IF`, `SUM`, `AVG`, `CONCAT`, `LEFT`, `ROUND`, and [many more](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/docs/formulas.md)\n-   **Relations & Lookups** — Link rows across databases and pull values from related notes\n-   **Advanced filters** — Type-aware operators with AND/OR logic\n-   **Live placeholders** — `{{column}}` tokens in a note body render the current cell value in reading view, updating as you edit the table\n-   **Auto-arrange** — Optionally file rows into nested subfolders driven by property values (`status=Done, priority=High` → `Done/High/row.md`)\n-   **7 languages** — English, Português (BR), Español, Français, Deutsch, 中文, 日本語\n-   **100% local Markdown** — Every row is a `.md` file, every column is a frontmatter field. No lock-in, no cloud, no telemetry\n\n---\n\n## Why Notion Bases?\n\n[](#why-notion-bases)\n\nObsidian's built-in Bases plugin is great for tables and has its own expression-based formula system. Notion Bases focuses on a different set of trade-offs — more views, more column types, and a spreadsheet-style formula syntax.\n\n### Views\n\n[](#views)\n\nView\n\nNotion Bases\n\nCore Bases\n\nTable\n\nYes\n\nYes\n\nBoard / Kanban\n\n**Yes**\n\nNo\n\nGallery\n\n**Yes**\n\nNo\n\nList\n\nYes\n\nYes\n\nCalendar\n\n**Yes**\n\nNo\n\nTimeline / Gantt\n\n**Yes**\n\nNo\n\nChart view\n\n**Yes**\n\nNo\n\n> Notion Bases offers **5 exclusive views** that Core Bases doesn't have — Board, Gallery, Calendar, Timeline, and Chart — giving you the flexibility to visualize data the way that fits your workflow.\n\n### Data modeling\n\n[](#data-modeling)\n\nFeature\n\nNotion Bases\n\nCore Bases\n\nColumn types\n\n**18**\n\n6\n\nFormulas\n\nSpreadsheet-style (`IF`, `SUM`, `AVG`, `CONCAT`)\n\nExpression-based (JS-like)\n\nRelation columns\n\n**Yes**\n\nNo\n\nLookup columns\n\n**Yes**\n\nNo\n\nRollup columns\n\n**Yes**\n\nNo\n\nImage columns\n\n**Rendered in cell**\n\nText only\n\nSubtasks / Sub-rows\n\n**Yes**\n\nNo\n\nNumber formatting (prefix, suffix, decimals, thousands)\n\n**Yes**\n\nNo\n\n> With relation and lookup columns, you can link databases together and pull values across notes — just like Notion. The spreadsheet-style formula syntax is familiar to anyone who has used Excel or Google Sheets.\n\n### Table experience\n\n[](#table-experience)\n\nFeature\n\nNotion Bases\n\nCore Bases\n\nColumn reordering (drag)\n\nYes\n\nYes\n\nColumn resizing (drag)\n\nYes\n\nYes\n\nColumn pinning\n\n**Yes**\n\nNo\n\nRow height options\n\nYes\n\nYes\n\nText wrap toggle\n\n**Yes**\n\nNo\n\nAggregation row\n\n**5 functions always visible**\n\nRight-click → Summarize\n\nMulti-column sort with priority\n\n**Yes**\n\nBasic sort\n\nCSV import / export\n\n**Yes**\n\nNo\n\nBulk actions (delete, duplicate, move)\n\n**Yes**\n\nNo\n\n> Both plugins let you resize, reorder columns and adjust row height. Notion Bases goes further with **column pinning**, **text wrap**, a **persistent aggregation footer**, **multi-column sort with drag-to-reorder priority**, **CSV import/export**, and **bulk row actions**.\n\n### Shared features\n\n[](#shared-features)\n\nFeature\n\nNotion Bases\n\nCore Bases\n\nEmbed database in any note\n\nYes\n\nYes\n\nMultiple views per database\n\nYes\n\nYes\n\nAND/OR filter logic\n\nYes\n\nYes\n\n100% local Markdown\n\nYes\n\nYes\n\n**If you ever wished Obsidian had Notion-level databases without leaving your vault, this is it.**\n\n---\n\n## Views\n\n[](#views-1)\n\n### Table\n\n[](#table)\n\nA fully interactive spreadsheet: inline editing, resizable/reorderable/pinnable columns, aggregation footer, row height options, text wrap, multi-column sort, and bulk row actions.\n\n[![Table view](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/raw/main/docs/images/view-table.png)](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/docs/images/view-table.png)\n\n### Board (Kanban)\n\n[](#board-kanban)\n\nDrag cards between columns grouped by any `select` or `status` field. Add cards directly to a column. Hide empty or no-value columns. Configure which properties appear on each card.\n\n[![Board view](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/raw/main/docs/images/view-board.png)](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/docs/images/view-board.png)\n\n[![Board drag](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/raw/main/docs/images/feature-board-drag.gif)](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/docs/images/feature-board-drag.gif)\n\n### Gallery\n\n[](#gallery)\n\nA responsive card grid. Pick a cover field, choose card size (small / medium / large), and display any properties below the title.\n\n[![Gallery view](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/raw/main/docs/images/view-gallery.png)](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/docs/images/view-gallery.png)\n\n### List\n\n[](#list)\n\nA minimal, single-line view — title plus property chips. Great for quick overviews and task-oriented databases.\n\n[![List view](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/raw/main/docs/images/view-list.png)](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/docs/images/view-list.png)\n\n### Calendar\n\n[](#calendar)\n\nMonthly calendar. Position notes by any `date` field. Click a day to create a note with the date pre-filled. Notes without a date appear in a collapsible section.\n\n[![Calendar view](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/raw/main/docs/images/view-calendar.png)](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/docs/images/view-calendar.png)\n\n### Timeline (Gantt)\n\n[](#timeline-gantt)\n\nHorizontal bar chart with three zoom levels (days / weeks / months). Drag bar edges to resize start or end dates. Group rows by any field.\n\n[![Timeline view](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/raw/main/docs/images/view-timeline.png)](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/docs/images/view-timeline.png)\n\n[![Timeline resize](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/raw/main/docs/images/feature-timeline-resize.gif)](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/docs/images/feature-timeline-resize.gif)\n\n### Chart\n\n[](#chart)\n\nBar, line, and pie charts rendered as pure SVG. Pick a category column (X axis), choose count or a number column (Y axis), and select an aggregation function. Smart axis formatting with k/M suffixes and integer ticks. Responsive sizing and full mobile support.\n\n[![Chart view](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/raw/main/docs/images/view-chart.png)](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/docs/images/view-chart.png)\n\n---\n\n## Features\n\n[](#features)\n\nCategory\n\nWhat you get\n\n**Column types**\n\nTitle, Text, Number, Select, Multi-select, Checkbox, Date, URL, Email, Phone, Status, Formula, Relation, Lookup, Rollup, Image, Audio, Video\n\n**Formulas**\n\n`IF`, `SUM`, `AVG`, `CONCAT`, `LEFT`, `ROUND` and [more](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/docs/formulas.md)\n\n**Relations & Lookups**\n\nLink rows across databases, pull values from related notes\n\n**Rollup**\n\nAggregate values across related databases: sum, count, avg, min, max, count\\_values, list\n\n**Charts**\n\nBar, line, pie — pure SVG with aggregations and smart axis formatting\n\n**Subtasks**\n\nHierarchical rows with expand/collapse up to 3 levels via self-relations\n\n**Filters**\n\nType-aware operators, AND/OR groups\n\n**Sorts**\n\nMulti-column with priority ordering\n\n**Aggregation**\n\nSum, Average, Min, Max, Count — updates live\n\n**Number formatting**\n\nPrefix (`$`, `R$`), suffix (`%`, `kg`), decimals, thousands separator\n\n**Column controls**\n\nPin, resize (drag), reorder (drag)\n\n**CSV**\n\nImport and export\n\n**Bulk actions**\n\nSelect rows to delete, duplicate or move\n\n**Schema inference**\n\nAuto-detects column types from existing frontmatter\n\n**Embeds**\n\nEmbed any database inside a note via code block — free multi-view or pinned to any view type\n\n**Multi-view**\n\nEach view has independent filters, sorts and field visibility\n\n**Live placeholders**\n\n`{{column}}` tokens in note bodies resolve to cell values in reading view\n\n**Folder arrangement**\n\nAuto-file rows into subfolders by property values, with batch preview\n\n**i18n**\n\nFull UI translation in 7 languages (en, pt-BR, es, fr, de, zh, ja)\n\n**100% Markdown**\n\nEvery row is a `.md` file. No lock-in, ever\n\n[![Inline editing](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/raw/main/docs/images/feature-inline-edit.gif)](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/docs/images/feature-inline-edit.gif)\n\n[![Filters](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/raw/main/docs/images/feature-filter.gif)](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/docs/images/feature-filter.gif)\n\n---\n\n## Column types\n\n[](#column-types)\n\nType\n\nDescription\n\n`title`\n\nNote filename — always the first column\n\n`text`\n\nPlain text\n\n`number`\n\nNumeric value with optional formatting\n\n`select`\n\nSingle option from a defined list\n\n`multiselect`\n\nMultiple options\n\n`checkbox`\n\nBoolean true / false\n\n`date`\n\nDate value\n\n`url`\n\nClickable link\n\n`email`\n\nEmail address\n\n`phone`\n\nPhone number\n\n`status`\n\nColored badge with inline management\n\n`formula`\n\nComputed value from other columns\n\n`relation`\n\nLink to a note in another database\n\n`lookup`\n\nPull a field from a related database\n\n`image`\n\nDisplay an image from the vault\n\n`rollup`\n\nAggregate values from related databases\n\n`audio`\n\nInline audio player with folder-based file picker\n\n`video`\n\nVideo with modal player and folder-based file picker\n\n---\n\n## Getting started\n\n[](#getting-started)\n\n### Installation\n\n[](#installation)\n\n**Via Community Plugins (recommended)**\n\nNotion Bases is available in Obsidian's Community Plugins directory:\n\n1.  Open **Settings → Community plugins → Browse**\n2.  Search for **\"Notion Bases\"**\n3.  Click **Install**, then **Enable**\n\nOr install it in one click from your browser: [open in Obsidian](https://obsidian.md/plugins?id=notion-bases).\n\n**Manual installation**\n\n1.  Download `main.js`, `manifest.json` and `styles.css` from the [latest release](https://github.com/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/releases/latest)\n2.  Create `<your-vault>/.obsidian/plugins/notion-bases/`\n3.  Copy the three files into it\n4.  Reload Obsidian and enable the plugin in **Settings → Community plugins**\n\n### Create your first database\n\n[](#create-your-first-database)\n\n1.  Open the command palette (`Ctrl/Cmd + P`) → **\"Create new database\"**\n2.  Pick a folder — a `_database.md` file marks it as a database\n3.  Click the table icon in the ribbon (or run **\"Open database\"**) to open it\n\n### Add views\n\n[](#add-views)\n\nClick **+** in the view tab bar to add a new view. Each view has its own filters, sorts and field visibility. Drag tabs to reorder.\n\n### Embed in a note\n\n[](#embed-in-a-note)\n\n\\`\\`\\`nb-database\npath: Projects\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nPin a fixed view type (no tabs) — any of `table`, `list`, `board`, `gallery`, `calendar`, `timeline` or `chart`:\n\n\\`\\`\\`nb-database\npath: Projects\ntype: board\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nA pinned embed inherits its configuration (board grouping, calendar date column, …) from the matching view defined in the database, so different notes can show the same data as a board, a calendar or a chart.\n\n[![Embed in note](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/raw/main/docs/images/feature-embed.png)](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/docs/images/feature-embed.png)\n\n---\n\n## How data is stored\n\n[](#how-data-is-stored)\n\nEverything lives in your vault as plain Markdown:\n\nWhat\n\nWhere\n\nRows\n\n`.md` files in the database folder\n\nColumn values\n\nFrontmatter fields in each note\n\nSchema & view config\n\nFrontmatter of `_database.md`\n\nEmbed view configs\n\nFrontmatter of the hosting note\n\nOpen any file in any text editor and your data is right there.\n\n---\n\n## Requirements\n\n[](#requirements)\n\n-   Obsidian `1.8.7` or later\n-   Desktop and mobile supported\n\n---\n\n## Support the project\n\n[](#support-the-project)\n\nIf Notion Bases makes your vault more powerful, consider supporting development:\n\n[![GitHub Sponsors](https://camo.githubusercontent.)](https://github.com/sponsors/bgarciamoura) [![Buy Me a Coffee](https://camo.githubusercontent.)](https://buymeacoffee.com/bgarciamoura)\n\n---\n\n## Contributing\n\n[](#contributing)\n\nContributions are welcome! Please read the [Contributing Guide](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) before submitting a pull request.\n\nFor bugs and feature requests, use the [issue tracker](https://github.com/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/issues).\n\n---\n\n## License\n\n[](#license)\n\n[GPL v3](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/blob/main/LICENSE) — free to use and modify, but any distribution must remain open source under the same license.\n\n## About\n\nTurn any folder into a Notion-style database — 7 views, 17 column types, formulas, relations, rollups, and subtasks. All stored in plain Markdown frontmatter.\n\n[bgarciamoura.github.io/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/](https://bgarciamoura.github.io/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/)\n\n### Topics\n\n[calendar](/topics/calendar)[charts](/topics/charts)[database](/topics/database)[frontmatter](/topics/frontmatter)[gallery](/topics/gallery)[kanban](/topics/kanban)[markdown](/topics/markdown)[notion](/topics/notion)[obsidian](/topics/obsidian)[obsidian-plugin](/topics/obsidian-plugin)[timeline](/topics/timeline)\n\n### Resources\n\n[Readme](#readme-ov-file)\n\n[GPL-3.0 license](#GPL-3.0-1-ov-file)\n\n### Code of conduct\n\n[Code of conduct](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin#coc-ov-file)\n\n### Contributing\n\n[Contributing](#contributing-ov-file)\n\n### Security policy\n\n[Security policy](#security-ov-file)\n\n[Activity](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/activity)\n\n### Stars\n\n**134** stars\n\n### Watchers\n\n**3** watching\n\n### Forks\n\n[**10** forks](/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin/forks)\n\n[Report repository](/contact/report-content?content_url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fbgarciamoura%2Fobsidian-notion-bases-plugin&report=bgarciamoura+%28user%29)\n\n## Releases\n\n## Packages\n\n## Contributors\n\n## Languages\n\n## Footer\n\n[](https://github.com)© 2026 GitHub, Inc.\n\n### Footer navigation\n\n-   [Terms](https://docs.github.com/site-policy/github-terms/github-terms-of-service)\n-   [Privacy](https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement)\n-   [Security](https://github.com/security)\n-   [Status](https://www.githubstatus.com/)\n-   [Community](https://github.community/)\n-   [Docs](https://docs.github.com/)\n-   [Contact](https://support.github.com?tags=dotcom-footer)\n-   Manage cookies\n-   Do not share my personal information\n\nYou can’t perform that action at this time.","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"https://github.com/bgarciamoura/obsidian-notion-bases-plugin (text/html; charset=utf-8)","time":{"start":1787344369788,"end":1787344370523}},"id":"prt_02606b76f0016mtkv3JvIyecTw","sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","messageID":"msg_026069e810017dcOb4Lpri09x6"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1787344371966,"sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","part":{"id":"prt_02606c0fc001kaT3aV0KsH0QN1","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","messageID":"msg_026069e810017dcOb4Lpri09x6","sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":127591,"input":4541,"output":103,"reasoning":67,"cache":{"write":0,"read":122880}},"cost":0.001027404}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1787344378328,"sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","part":{"id":"prt_02606d9d0001rpLjz2HcV6NUGr","messageID":"msg_02606c6ff001RL591eUfgwKO4T","sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787344403245,"sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_005f9be9d65f4807a0b04f39","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/mcp-tooling/015-notion-to-obisidian-migration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md","content":"# Iteration 1: mcp-notion-reads / mcp-obsidian-writes Division of Labor — Inventory and Import Steps\n\n## Focus\nMap every migration step (inventory, import, reconstruction, verification) to the exact mcp-notion or mcp-obsidian tool surface that performs it.\n\n## Findings\n\n### F1.1 — Inventory Phase: mcp-notion owns all reads\n\nThe pre-flight inventory requires enumerating every Notion page, database/data source, property, relation, rollup, formula, view, comment, and file. The 24 mcp-notion tools cover every read operation needed:\n\n| Inventory item | mcp-notion tool | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| List all pages by title | `search` | Title-only search — no full-text content search |\n| Retrieve page content (body) | `retrieve-page-markdown` | Token-efficient; returns full Markdown body |\n| Retrieve page metadata/properties | `retrieve-a-page` | Properties only; 25-item truncation on relation/people/rich_text fields |\n| List database data sources | `retrieve-a-database` | Returns container metadata + data source IDs |\n| Get data source schema | `retrieve-a-data-source` | Returns property definitions, types, and options |\n| Query rows | `query-data-source` | Filter + sort + pagination; retrieves all rows |\n| List comments | `list-comments` | Per-page unresolved comments list |\n| List views | Direct API (Gap 2) | MCP has no view tool — `GET /v1/databases/{id}/views` needed |\n| Retrieve property items (non-truncated) | Direct API (Gap 3) | `GET /v1/pages/{id}/properties/{prop}` for relation/people fields with >25 references |\n| List users | `list-all-users` | For audit purposes |\n\n[SOURCE: mcp-notion SKILL.md §3 — 24-tool catalog, 5 API gaps]\n[SOURCE: mcp-notion/references/mcp-tools.md §5 — tool inventory]\n[SOURCE: mcp-notion/references/api-gap-tools.md §4-5 — views and property items]\n\n### F1.2 — Import Phase: Human-driven, but mcp-obsidian handles post-import\n\nThe official Obsidian Importer (in-app UI) performs the actual Import step — it is NOT a programmatic surface the AI can call. The AI's role is:\n\n1. **Human action**: Open Obsidian → Importer → \"Notion (API)\" → paste internal integration token → select scope → run\n2. **AI layer after import**: mcp-obsidian (notesmd-cli or MCP) reads/verifies/writes the resulting vault files\n\n[SOURCE: prior-findings.md §5 — human runs the Importer; agent works around it]\n[SOURCE: mcp-obsidian SKILL.md §3 — notesmd-cli operates filesystem, MCP operates live vault]\n\n### F1.3 — mcp-obsidian Write Surface for Post-Import Tasks\n\n| Post-import task | mcp-obsidian surface | Tool/command | Requires running app? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Read imported note | MCP (app) / CLI (headless) | `obsidian_get_note` / `notesmd-cli print` | MCP: Yes / CLI: No |\n| Write/overwrite note | MCP (app) / CLI (headless) | `obsidian_write_note` / `notesmd-cli create` | MCP: Yes / CLI: No |\n| Edit frontmatter | CLI (headless) | `notesmd-cli frontmatter` | No |\n| Search notes by name | CLI (headless) | `notesmd-cli list` + filter | No |\n| Full-text search | CLI (headless) | `notesmd-cli search-content` | No |\n| Global search (live vault) | MCP (app) | `obsidian_search_notes` | Yes |\n| Manage tags | MCP (app) | `obsidian_manage_tags` | Yes |\n| Delete note | MCP / CLI | `obsidian_delete_note` / `notesmd-cli delete` | Varies |\n| Plugin-driven tasks | Reference | Dataview, Tables, etc. | Plugins loaded |\n\n[SOURCE: mcp-obsidian SKILL.md §2 — operation-to-tool routing table]\n[SOURCE: mcp-obsidian/references/mcp-tools.md §5 — 14 MCP tool surface]\n\n### F1.4 — The mcp-notion Read Surface Has Critical Gaps for Inventory\n\n1. **Title-only search** — `search` returns only title matches; full-text content search is impossible via the Notion API. For a complete inventory, must iterate all pages by traversing the root page tree.\n2. **25-reference truncation** — `retrieve-a-page` truncates relation/people/rich_text at 25 references. To get the full set, must call the property-item endpoint per property (Gap 3).\n3. **Views are read-only via MCP** — creating/reading views requires direct Notion API calls (Gap 2). The MCP's `query-data-source` can replicate filtered reads, but cannot read the saved view configuration.\n4. **No file/attachment enumeration** — Notion files are embedded in blocks or `files` properties. Inventory requires reading each page's Markdown body (via `retrieve-page-markdown`) to detect file references, plus calling file-upload endpoints (Gap 1) for upload metadata.\n\n[SOURCE: mcp-notion/references/mcp-tools.md §7 — 5 uncovered domains]\n[SOURCE: mcp-notion/references/api-gap-tools.md — direct API recipes]\n\n## Sources Consulted\n- mcp-notion SKILL.md\n- mcp-obsidian SKILL.md\n- mcp-notion/references/mcp-tools.md\n- mcp-notion/references/api-gap-tools.md\n- mcp-obsidian/references/mcp-tools.md\n- prior-findings.md\n- Obsidian Help — Import from Notion: https://obsidian.md/help/import/notion\n- Notion API Reference: https://developers.notion.com/reference\n\n## Assessment\n- newInfoRatio: 1.0\n- noveltyJustification: \"First pass on tool-surface mapping; entirely new evidence not in prior-findings\"\n- Confidence: High — all tool names and capabilities are source-confirmed from skill references\n- This iteration answered the structural question of which tool does what, but raised four sub-questions on gaps\n\n## Reflection\n- What worked: Reading both skill SKILL.md files and tool references side-by-side produced a decisive tool-per-step map\n- What failed: The Importer UI is opaque to AI — confirmed this is a human-only step\n- Ruled out: Using mcp-notion for post-import vault writes (mcp-obsidian owns that surface entirely)\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\nKQ-3 continued: Deep-dive on the reconstruction and verification steps — specifically how mcp-obsidian rebuilds relations, creates .base files, and writes Dataview queries."},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/mcp-tooling/015-notion-to-obisidian-migration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"specs/mcp-tooling/015-notion-to-obisidian-migration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md","time":{"start":1787344403230,"end":1787344403243}},"id":"prt_02606e066001yw8w3bPlNlbRMZ","sessionID":"ses_fd9fbd8f6ffe5QlvbFKBCh0T14","messageID":"msg_02606c6ff001RL591eUfgwKO4T"}}
